WEBVTT

00:38.970 --> 00:41.280
Hello there, boys and girls.

00:41.280 --> 00:44.750
I'm Lolo! I'm a soft and fluffy bear!

00:44.750 --> 00:50.170
And I'm Mimuji! I come from a long line of vikings, or pirates!

00:50.170 --> 00:52.750
Aren't vikings and pirates completely different things?

00:52.750 --> 00:55.380
Don't sweat the details, just continue talking.

00:55.380 --> 00:57.050
Tell 'em a fun story!

00:57.050 --> 00:58.730
Sure thing, Mimuji.

01:00.430 --> 01:07.920
Once upon a time, there was a village called Musashino Animation where they made animation.

01:09.600 --> 01:13.380
The people who lived there were so free-spirited

01:13.380 --> 01:15.880
that there was always some trouble going on.

01:16.590 --> 01:17.780
I'm out of ideas!

01:18.880 --> 01:24.240
But then along came someone who said,
"Things can't go on like this."

01:24.240 --> 01:27.850
It was a small girl called Meowmori.

01:44.500 --> 01:47.250
Musashino Animation

01:50.500 --> 01:55.510
Meowmori cheered everyone on,
and they were able to make a bit of anime.

01:55.510 --> 01:58.580
But just a bit isn't enough.

01:58.580 --> 02:03.430
If they didn't complete all of it,
they wouldn't get to have dinner.

02:03.430 --> 02:06.430
Meowmori went to find people who would help.

02:06.810 --> 02:08.110
Hey!

02:07.280 --> 02:11.650
She comforted a crybaby, and captured slackers.

02:11.960 --> 02:15.490
The screenwriter said that the script was done,

02:15.490 --> 02:19.420
and the director said that the storyboards were done.

02:19.420 --> 02:24.990
The script and the storyboard—
never mind how it looks—are the blueprints of anime.

02:25.350 --> 02:28.040
"Time to draw!" said the animators.

02:29.750 --> 02:32.250
"Time to color it!" said the coloring staff,

02:32.250 --> 02:34.750
"Time to make some CG!" said the 3D artists,

02:34.750 --> 02:36.880
"Time to paint backgrounds!" said the background artists,

02:36.880 --> 02:39.510
"Time to film it!" said the filming staff.

02:39.860 --> 02:42.510
"Time to record the voices!" said the voice actors,

02:42.510 --> 02:46.890
and "Time to do the music and SFX!"
said the composer and sound effects staff.

02:49.820 --> 02:50.920
This way!

02:51.580 --> 02:57.360
But then, funny story, someone from the publisher came and said, "Doesn't this part look weird?"

02:57.360 --> 03:00.380
Funny story, I can't let this slide, yo.

03:00.380 --> 03:02.620
You better redo it all from scratch, yo.

03:09.930 --> 03:13.170
But Meowmori and her team refused to give up.

03:14.900 --> 03:17.300
They hashed everything out with the author, and...

03:26.360 --> 03:30.770
They worked hard to create a good anime until the very end.

03:30.770 --> 03:31.880
And finally...

03:32.690 --> 03:35.770
They completed a wonderful anime.

03:38.920 --> 03:39.980
This way!

03:56.020 --> 03:59.390
They all held toasts with smiles on their faces.

03:59.390 --> 04:03.200
The hot-heads, the slackers,
the cool cucumbers and the crybabies...

04:03.200 --> 04:05.640
Every single one of them was smiling.

04:06.020 --> 04:09.290
And then they all lived happily ever after.

04:09.290 --> 04:09.910
What?

04:09.910 --> 04:13.070
They all became rich and famous,

04:13.070 --> 04:16.180
fell in love, and are super happy, right?

04:16.180 --> 04:17.840
Um...

04:18.810 --> 04:22.280
This movie is about what happened four years later.

04:22.280 --> 04:23.760
Four years, huh?

04:23.760 --> 04:26.490
How's everyone doing? Tell me, tell me!

04:33.460 --> 04:37.340
April 2019

04:39.440 --> 04:43.830
That was a letter from "Sergeant Anime."
Thank you for writing.

04:43.830 --> 04:47.780
Well, yeah, I suppose the number of anime shows may or may not have declined lately.

04:47.780 --> 04:52.500
I mean, I always record basically every anime I can,
and I'm still able to keep up no problem this season.

04:52.500 --> 04:54.850
Just goes to show how few there are, huh?

04:54.850 --> 04:57.660
The anime bubble's burst, leaving a barren wasteland.

04:57.660 --> 05:01.570
And I hear Blu-rays haven't been selling at all lately.

05:00.300 --> 05:02.990
Now, now, let's forget about scary realities like that,

05:02.990 --> 05:04.160
and talk about you-know-what.

05:04.160 --> 05:05.590
What? Oh, that.

05:05.590 --> 05:08.730
We, Anime Radio Lazy Revolution, will be talking about...

05:08.730 --> 05:11.420
Ta-da! Magical Oyster!

05:11.420 --> 05:14.500
And in fact, the person playing
Magical Oyster is here with us today!

05:13.500 --> 05:15.170
Yay!

05:14.500 --> 05:17.460
Or so I'd like to say, but we were turned down.

05:17.460 --> 05:20.830
Except that's a lie, we don't have the budget for guests to begin with!

05:20.830 --> 05:21.520
I'm serious.

05:21.520 --> 05:22.880
Life is hard, huh...

05:22.880 --> 05:25.830
But we're still huge fans of Magical Oyster.

05:25.830 --> 05:30.180
Now let's go to an oldie but goodie,
our first song for tonight!

05:30.180 --> 05:33.180
It's the opening theme to
Aging Village Depopulation Girl:

05:33.180 --> 05:35.670
"We Don't Have a Choice, So What'cha Gonna Do?"

05:46.650 --> 05:51.690
We smile and get along with each other

05:51.690 --> 05:57.230
We teeter and bottle up our frustrations

05:57.230 --> 06:02.300
Feels like we're going round and round and round

06:02.300 --> 06:06.930
Always ending up back where we started

06:08.520 --> 06:11.950
Back where we started

06:12.510 --> 06:18.670
That's just how it goes, how it goes

06:18.670 --> 06:22.920
What can you do?

06:24.850 --> 06:30.040
We think it through real hard and get light-headed

06:30.040 --> 06:35.410
We stumble around as we try to fight the dizziness

06:35.410 --> 06:40.640
In the end all we do is make a lot of noise

06:40.640 --> 06:46.060
That's why we're stuck where we are

06:46.660 --> 06:50.190
Stuck where we are

06:50.700 --> 06:56.340
That's just how it goes, how it goes

06:57.160 --> 07:00.760
What can you do?

07:01.200 --> 07:05.420
Everyone's gone

07:11.170 --> 07:16.200
There's an itch behind my forehead

07:16.580 --> 07:22.570
That itch is what makes me so pensive

07:23.660 --> 07:29.460
That's just how it goes, how it goes

07:30.260 --> 07:34.580
What can you do?

07:35.420 --> 07:38.270
Even if it's all for naught

07:38.270 --> 07:43.700
What can you do?

08:06.560 --> 08:07.860
Miyamori?

08:11.240 --> 08:13.730
3rd Wing is about to start.

08:13.730 --> 08:15.290
Don't you want to see it?

08:16.490 --> 08:18.700
Oh yeah, today's our episode.

08:18.700 --> 08:20.190
Aren't you excited?

08:22.160 --> 08:25.220
Oh, you can go ahead. I'll catch up later.

08:25.220 --> 08:26.300
Okay!

08:45.400 --> 08:48.170
Oh, Miyamori! Come get some curry!

08:48.170 --> 08:50.870
It's my special anime-watching curry.

08:49.850 --> 08:51.380
Meowmori, over here!

08:50.870 --> 08:51.920
It's just about to begin.

08:51.920 --> 08:53.470
We were waiting for you, Miyamori.

08:53.470 --> 08:54.980
Miyamori, you're such a workaholic.

08:54.980 --> 08:56.680
It's done? Awesome job, Miyamori.

08:56.680 --> 08:57.550
Well done.

08:57.550 --> 08:59.180
Didn't take you long, Miyamori.

08:59.180 --> 09:01.180
Looking forward to the airing, Miyamori?

09:01.180 --> 09:02.700
I'm kind of nervous...

09:02.700 --> 09:05.350
I'm sure it turned out well, Miyamori.

09:05.350 --> 09:07.860
We're really indebted to Miyamori, huh?

09:07.860 --> 09:08.230
Miya!

09:08.230 --> 09:09.610
Hi, Oi, wanna sit with me?

09:26.960 --> 09:27.000
3rd Girls' Fighter Wing

09:33.420 --> 09:34.260
Scramble!

09:36.840 --> 09:37.970
No!

09:42.440 --> 09:44.600
No, stop!

09:46.140 --> 09:48.120
No way!

09:48.120 --> 09:51.200
I was expecting way too much realism from the aircraft.

09:51.200 --> 09:55.420
It's 3rd Wing II, after all. No point in
overthinking the action with this kind of show.

09:55.420 --> 09:56.790
Hm? "This kind of show"?

09:56.790 --> 09:59.880
It's still annoying that the director overrode my decisions.

09:59.880 --> 10:02.390
But it's a bit fun how over the top it is, isn't it?

10:02.390 --> 10:04.850
Do you have it out for me, Satou?

10:04.850 --> 10:07.540
If only Musani were the lead studio...

10:09.190 --> 10:10.810
By the way, where's NabeP?

10:10.810 --> 10:12.170
That's NabePrez now, remember?

10:12.170 --> 10:17.510
Oh yeah, that's right. So where might our esteemed president Watanabe Shun be?

10:14.760 --> 10:17.510
Mahjong

10:14.760 --> 10:17.510
Standard

10:18.030 --> 10:19.470
Look, 3rd Wing II's on.

10:19.470 --> 10:21.490
A season two after four years?

10:21.490 --> 10:23.440
Good job getting that through, Gou.

10:23.440 --> 10:28.270
Nah, we may be producing it,
but I'm not in charge of it, so I'm hands off.

10:28.270 --> 10:29.530
Huh, really?

10:29.530 --> 10:31.230
I don't remember 3rd Wing being like this...

10:31.230 --> 10:33.720
And we're not making it, either.

10:33.720 --> 10:34.360
Oh my.

10:34.360 --> 10:37.610
Not that we'd have any chance of being a lead studio right now.

10:37.610 --> 10:41.320
I'm amazed you accepted the offer,
Madoka. Oh, I meant that as a compliment.

10:41.320 --> 10:45.090
Most people wouldn't accept work on a show they used to be the lead studio for.

10:41.320 --> 10:47.960
Medusa

10:45.090 --> 10:47.960
Come on, it's not like I don't have any love for the show.

10:47.960 --> 10:52.720
Next time on 3rd Girls' Fighter Wing Medusa: "A Mackarel Can and a Rondo of Sorrow."

10:51.000 --> 10:55.590
A Mackarel Can and a Rondo of Sorrow

10:52.720 --> 10:55.590
I'll Master Arm On your heart!

10:55.590 --> 10:57.880
Let's see what people are... Or let's not, actually.

10:57.880 --> 11:00.450
You're talking like Director Kinoshita.

11:00.450 --> 11:01.810
Have you met up with him lately?

11:01.810 --> 11:02.890
No, not at all.

11:02.890 --> 11:07.940
I heard from a credible source that Seiichi Kinoshita's
storyboards for Studio Nero were late the other day.

11:07.940 --> 11:10.020
He <i>did</i> deliver them in the end.

11:10.020 --> 11:12.780
But he stalled the work for quite some time.

11:12.780 --> 11:14.040
Why, that was terribly rude of me.

11:14.040 --> 11:17.960
Or so I heard from Andou,
the girl who went to Dropfit Studio.

11:17.960 --> 11:19.530
Oh, same place as Ochiai.

11:19.530 --> 11:23.930
But never mind Director Kinoshita,
can you believe Yamada?

11:23.930 --> 11:26.540
He hit it big with his debut as a director for Two Piece.

11:26.540 --> 11:30.750
In The Center of the World and
My Name are both huge hits at the cinemas, too.

11:30.750 --> 11:32.890
I read an interview with him the other day.

11:32.890 --> 11:34.290
He was wearing some weird get-up.

11:34.290 --> 11:35.380
Weird get-up?

11:35.380 --> 11:43.510
I want the viewers to get a glimpse of something akin to the hope that lies beyond despair.

11:35.380 --> 11:43.520
Animation Director

11:35.380 --> 11:43.520
Yamada Masashi

11:44.140 --> 11:46.590
Yamada sure learned to talk the talk.

11:46.590 --> 11:50.840
This must be promotion for his newest work,
Bride and Raven, premiering in September.

11:48.400 --> 11:57.740
Eyes Glued 365

11:50.840 --> 11:53.520
The advance tickets are selling well, I hear.

11:53.890 --> 11:55.540
Takahashi, are you a Yamada fan?

11:55.540 --> 11:57.730
Certainly not—this is simply common knowledge.

11:57.730 --> 11:59.010
Couldn't deny it any harder.

11:59.010 --> 12:02.220
Oh, I didn't mean it that way! I do like his work!

12:02.220 --> 12:06.590
You're like a parallel universe version of Takanashi.

12:06.590 --> 12:08.090
Is he someone who works at Musani?

12:08.090 --> 12:12.480
He used to work here as a production assistant.
Though he left Musani and became an episode director.

12:12.480 --> 12:14.380
But he's still as wild as ever.

12:14.380 --> 12:18.210
He had a great opportunity, but ruined it by getting into a fight with Director Mijikai.

12:18.210 --> 12:21.260
I don't think it's a "fight" if only the director got pissed off.

12:21.260 --> 12:23.850
He really thinks too highly of himself.

12:23.850 --> 12:25.740
Same as when he was an assistant.

12:25.740 --> 12:29.150
He sure is resilient though.
I wish Endou would take a leaf out of—

12:29.150 --> 12:32.500
Oh! Musani's Endou could only refer to one person, Endou Ryousuke!

12:32.500 --> 12:34.950
He's renowned for his action and effect animation!

12:33.910 --> 12:38.410
Miyamori, I'll be heading to Yumeinu Company
for a bit. Call me if you need anything.

12:38.410 --> 12:39.570
G-Got it!

12:39.570 --> 12:41.320
Tsumo. Chinroutou.

12:41.320 --> 12:45.080
Seriously?! This is my third time ever seeing a chinroutou!

12:45.080 --> 12:47.200
You better be careful, or you'll die an early death.

12:47.200 --> 12:50.290
Don't worry, wanting to die is my main job.

12:51.310 --> 12:54.330
Come on, where does that put me?

12:54.330 --> 12:56.360
I'm doing awful at both mahjong and my job.

12:56.360 --> 12:58.100
Oh, you're exaggerating.

12:58.100 --> 13:00.240
No, I mean it.

13:02.300 --> 13:03.590
Excuse me just a moment.

13:03.590 --> 13:05.270
Well aren't you the busy man?

13:11.650 --> 13:14.740
What in the world are you saying?! You promised me!

13:14.740 --> 13:16.950
Honestly, I can't believe you!

13:16.080 --> 13:19.840
That's my third time ever hearing Gou angry.

13:19.840 --> 13:21.110
That's him being angry?

13:21.110 --> 13:23.360
Sure is. Super angry.

13:23.360 --> 13:24.320
Seriously?

13:25.320 --> 13:28.200
Today's 3rd Wing II was something else, huh?

13:28.200 --> 13:31.910
Yeah, they're not even trying to hide that they're appealing to a male audience.

13:30.330 --> 13:31.910
I'm ba—

13:33.160 --> 13:35.290
You'll be there tomorrow, right?

13:35.680 --> 13:37.420
Yeah, probably.

13:37.420 --> 13:39.270
What time did we say again?

13:39.270 --> 13:39.940
What time...

13:39.940 --> 13:40.800
Seven!

13:40.800 --> 13:42.060
It's seven o'clock.

13:42.060 --> 13:43.780
Got it. I should be able to make it.

13:43.780 --> 13:44.880
That's great.

13:45.270 --> 13:47.180
Me? I'll be fine.

13:47.180 --> 13:49.340
It's been so long. No way I'm missing it.

13:50.020 --> 13:52.010
Yeah, though I won't be able to stay out drinking.

13:52.010 --> 13:53.290
Oh, not because of work.

13:53.290 --> 13:55.770
Lately I get tired whenever I drink.

13:56.330 --> 13:57.680
See you tomorrow.

13:58.920 --> 14:01.410
You didn't eat anything for lunch.

14:01.410 --> 14:02.270
Lunch?

14:02.820 --> 14:04.600
Oh! I completely forgot!

14:04.600 --> 14:07.400
You shouldn't forget. More important than work.

14:07.400 --> 14:11.740
But if I don't finish the layout checks,
the others can't get started with the keyframes.

14:11.740 --> 14:14.830
You haven't been able to do keyframe checks at all!

14:14.830 --> 14:17.850
Not enough time. Moved on without your approval.

14:17.850 --> 14:21.960
I'd like to look at the keyframes too if I could,
but it's not possible with the current schedule.

14:23.100 --> 14:24.920
Thank you for worrying, Kunogi.

14:25.410 --> 14:26.630
Thanks for the food.

14:31.360 --> 14:34.680
I'm so happy that I get to live with you.

14:35.270 --> 14:38.360
Having a separate bathroom and toilet is like a dream come true.

14:38.360 --> 14:39.580
And you cook for me too.

14:38.950 --> 14:41.150
No! I can't do cleaning!

14:41.150 --> 14:43.890
Really? I think it's pretty tidy here.

14:45.400 --> 14:47.030
Studio
Canabun

14:46.140 --> 14:48.060
How fast is this going?

14:48.060 --> 14:49.360
About 100 km/h, I guess.

14:49.360 --> 14:50.300
And the curve radius?

14:49.790 --> 14:51.640
Well, it's pretty sharp.

14:51.640 --> 14:54.850
Cornering a sharp curve at 100 km/h...

14:54.850 --> 14:57.500
Is it using strut or double wishbone suspension?

14:57.500 --> 14:58.420
Not sure...

14:58.420 --> 15:02.630
If you made this with the tire compound and
the type and structure of the suspension in mind

15:02.630 --> 15:06.460
it would never end up looking this weirdly smooth.

15:06.460 --> 15:08.760
I understand what you're saying, Toudou,

15:08.760 --> 15:11.410
but I don't have time to put that much effort into a filler scene!

15:11.410 --> 15:14.970
Yes, of course it's important to make it on time, but you can still—

15:13.890 --> 15:16.190
Delivery comes first for me.

15:16.190 --> 15:18.310
Besides, if you're aiming for realism,

15:18.310 --> 15:20.590
then why aren't you doing live action?

15:20.590 --> 15:22.440
It's important to set your priorities straight.

15:22.440 --> 15:27.150
Yeah, but there's a difference between knowing something
and not doing it, and just randomly doing whatever, right?

15:28.570 --> 15:30.650
Fine, I'll see what I can come up with.

15:32.080 --> 15:33.990
Okudo, how is your work coming along?

15:33.990 --> 15:37.310
I'm sorry, it's still too rough to show anyone.

15:37.310 --> 15:39.290
Would you mind if I still had a look?

15:41.640 --> 15:42.790
Um...

15:42.790 --> 15:45.770
I'm sorry. That's why I said it's still too rough.

15:45.770 --> 15:49.390
So... When do you think you'll be able to finish it?

15:49.390 --> 15:53.520
I can tell you're trying to be thorough,
but I do need to know when the delivery will be...

15:53.520 --> 15:55.420
When do you think it will be?

15:55.420 --> 15:55.970
Huh?

15:55.970 --> 15:58.350
Everything I do looks bad to me.

15:58.350 --> 16:01.750
I can't even tell myself when I might be done.

16:01.750 --> 16:06.740
Then why don't you show me what you have when you're 60% satisfied with your work?

16:06.740 --> 16:10.110
We'll discuss polishing and deadlines then.

16:10.110 --> 16:15.590
Imai, the line here goes "Aren't we comrades aiming for the same Paradia paradise?",

16:15.590 --> 16:19.960
so doesn't the subsequent "You really hate katsudon, huh?" flow kind of strange?

16:19.960 --> 16:24.250
I don't understand why there's a flashback right after they find their resolve.

16:21.000 --> 16:24.250
Maitake Shimeji
Writer

16:24.250 --> 16:28.000
Um, but... I wanted to stay true to the original.

16:28.000 --> 16:28.770
You're right.

16:28.770 --> 16:32.030
But if it bothers the viewers,
it doesn't matter how faithful you are.

16:32.030 --> 16:33.360
Yeah, that's true.

16:33.360 --> 16:35.820
Didn't you see the issue when you were writing?

16:35.820 --> 16:37.330
I hoped it would work.

16:37.330 --> 16:38.350
Did it?

16:52.240 --> 16:54.150
Depressing! This is just too depressing!

16:54.150 --> 16:56.640
Why? Why? Everyone was working so hard!

16:56.640 --> 16:58.390
Everyone was so happy!

16:58.390 --> 17:00.240
Well, the thing about life is...

17:00.240 --> 17:02.370
It doesn't always work out like you want!

17:02.370 --> 17:04.440
Wait, Lolo! What happened to you?!

17:04.440 --> 17:07.140
You're a super bear with a tummy full of love and dreams!

17:07.140 --> 17:11.430
That mark on your chest is a symbol of hope,
meant to one day turn into a full moon, right?!

17:11.430 --> 17:14.350
Pfft, it's nothing but a printing error.

17:23.230 --> 17:26.200
Hi, Aoi? It's your mom. Where are you?

17:26.200 --> 17:26.830
At home.

17:26.830 --> 17:27.920
You're home early.

17:27.920 --> 17:30.830
I just happened to get home early. What's up?

17:30.830 --> 17:31.400
Heya.

17:31.400 --> 17:33.550
Sis? What are you doing there?

17:33.550 --> 17:34.360
I got divorced.

17:34.360 --> 17:34.880
What?!

17:34.880 --> 17:36.420
Just kidding.

17:36.420 --> 17:38.610
Are you coming home over Golden Week?

17:38.610 --> 17:41.950
If you are, I'll have Haru's birthday party while you're here.

17:41.950 --> 17:44.360
Sis, should you really be letting him stay up this late?

17:44.360 --> 17:46.460
He just woke up. Didn't you?

17:46.460 --> 17:49.440
Well, I don't know when I'm free,
so go ahead and decide without me.

17:49.440 --> 17:50.500
Really? Okay.

17:50.500 --> 17:53.660
Must be nice to do what you like for a living.

17:53.660 --> 17:55.620
And you've got lots of work at that.

17:55.620 --> 17:57.270
I'm jealous.

18:01.100 --> 18:02.400
She just left home.

18:02.400 --> 18:04.600
As busy as ever, isn't she?

18:04.600 --> 18:06.810
Zuka, want some more beer?

18:06.810 --> 18:08.210
Oh, sure! Thank you!

18:08.210 --> 18:10.770
Come on, you don't work here anymore.
No need to be so polite!

18:10.770 --> 18:13.990
That's right. You're one of our valued customers.

18:14.590 --> 18:15.940
Thank you.

18:22.910 --> 18:23.830
Right.

18:24.420 --> 18:26.580
I'm here now! Sorry I'm late!

18:26.580 --> 18:28.680
Oh, there you are, Aoi! We were waiting for you!

18:27.260 --> 18:27.940
Been a while.

18:27.940 --> 18:29.430
Great timing!

18:28.680 --> 18:29.980
Did you finish your work?

18:29.980 --> 18:30.830
More or less!

18:30.830 --> 18:31.560
Now, then...

18:31.560 --> 18:32.840
Cheers!

18:39.520 --> 18:41.580
I was really looking forward to today!

18:41.580 --> 18:43.390
I've got so much I wanted to tell you guys!

18:43.390 --> 18:44.530
Me too! Me too!

18:44.530 --> 18:46.220
Bequeath thine tales, companions.

18:46.520 --> 18:51.030
I believe that you should work as hard as you can when you can,

18:51.030 --> 18:54.290
but it feels like others think I'm working too hard...

18:54.290 --> 18:56.330
But you still have to work hard.

18:56.330 --> 18:58.000
Yeah, I want to work as hard as I can.

18:58.000 --> 19:00.330
You can't just half-ass it, right?

19:00.330 --> 19:02.380
You never know when you might be out of work.

19:02.380 --> 19:04.760
What? But everything's been smooth sailing for you, Ri.

19:04.760 --> 19:07.370
You budding, enterprising, A-list screenwriter!

19:07.580 --> 19:10.480
No way! I'm not enterprising or an A-lister at all!

19:10.480 --> 19:13.380
I'm only able to manage because my master helps me get work.

19:13.380 --> 19:18.380
But you got put in charge of a show and wrote 12 episodes
all by yourself just two years after your debut, right?

19:18.380 --> 19:21.620
The Three Sisters of Petersburg! That was such a Ri show.

19:21.620 --> 19:24.640
Like the drama and banter between the characters, or the tragic ending.

19:24.640 --> 19:26.520
They called it a huge flop though.

19:26.520 --> 19:29.530
They say notoriety is better than obscurity!
Don't let it get to you.

19:29.530 --> 19:30.530
That's right!

19:30.530 --> 19:35.830
But if all I have is notoriety,
won't I start to lose work and be out of a job?

19:40.300 --> 19:42.040
Zuka, your show's about to start!

19:42.040 --> 19:42.760
What? How?

19:42.760 --> 19:44.380
We got cable!

19:44.380 --> 19:48.650
A customer told us that you were on Urawa TV!

19:48.650 --> 19:50.140
We've been watching every week!

19:50.140 --> 19:54.070
Upcoming anime! Storming the recording studio for a surprise interview!

19:54.070 --> 19:57.980
Today's show is known for its grim setting and borderline inappropriate gags!

19:56.880 --> 20:15.440
The anime on everyone's lips this season

19:56.880 --> 20:15.440
Peperumoko, the Guillotine CEO

19:57.980 --> 20:01.630
We'll be joining a recording of
Peperumoko, the Guillotine CEO!

20:01.630 --> 20:06.870
Even many adults find adding voices to animation difficult. How are you getting along, Mone?

20:06.870 --> 20:09.390
Well, it's my job, so I'm fine.

20:10.720 --> 20:12.890
Are you a voice actor, Miss Sasaki?

20:12.890 --> 20:15.440
Well... Yes, more or less.

20:17.940 --> 20:20.120
Mone was so tiny and cute!

20:20.120 --> 20:21.740
She's got intuition and guts too!

20:21.740 --> 20:24.560
Her mother told her to stop being so introverted

20:24.560 --> 20:27.890
and made her do fifty retakes the first time, she said!

20:27.890 --> 20:31.250
Can you believe that?
If it was me, I'd have run out the door!

20:32.680 --> 20:38.670
The five of us chased after our dreams
and made them our jobs.

20:38.670 --> 20:42.170
But how much closer are we to making the Seven Lucky Warriors?

21:16.300 --> 21:19.190
I'm sorry I can't help out at Musani.

21:19.190 --> 21:22.420
Don't worry about it! Not like there's any work to do at Musani anyway.

21:22.940 --> 21:26.180
I think you did the right thing in going elsewhere.

21:26.180 --> 21:29.500
But I'm definitely having you
join up next time we do something!

21:29.500 --> 21:30.930
Yeah! I'll do it!

21:31.200 --> 21:34.410
I'd like to have Ogasawara and Iguchi help out too...

21:34.410 --> 21:36.380
And Kunogi too, of course!

21:40.040 --> 21:42.400
Sorry, I gotta take this call. See you!

21:46.620 --> 21:48.570
Hello, this is Miyamori.

21:47.330 --> 21:49.410
You picked up!

21:50.090 --> 21:52.100
I can't get ahold of Nabe!

21:52.100 --> 21:54.290
Huh? He said he was heading straight home.

21:54.290 --> 21:56.350
At a time like this?!

21:56.350 --> 21:59.810
I can't take living anymore! I want to die!

21:58.500 --> 21:59.380
What?!

21:59.810 --> 22:02.710
Or maybe I'll kill him first and then die!

22:00.880 --> 22:02.710
Katsuragi?!

22:02.710 --> 22:05.070
Don't do anything you'll regret!

22:05.070 --> 22:06.880
This isn't about Nabe, just so we're clear.

22:07.260 --> 22:11.790
Miyamori, what should I do?!

22:11.790 --> 22:15.320
Well... How about living, for starters?

22:15.970 --> 22:18.770
All right. I'll try.

22:23.530 --> 22:24.780
Was there anything else?

22:26.520 --> 22:28.910
If not, I'm concluding today's morning meeting.

22:30.340 --> 22:31.740
Miyamori, got some time?

22:31.740 --> 22:32.750
Sure.

22:32.750 --> 22:34.240
I'm going out for a bit. Come with me.

22:37.220 --> 22:40.010
I'm pretty sure there's a meeting room open.

22:40.010 --> 22:42.680
I don't like being at the studio.

22:45.310 --> 22:47.630
Does it have something to do with Katsuragi?

22:48.610 --> 22:50.570
Can't hide anything from our ace, huh?

22:50.570 --> 22:52.220
I don't like the way you said that.

22:55.500 --> 22:56.670
Welcome!

22:56.670 --> 22:58.370
Oh, it's you two.

22:58.370 --> 22:59.780
Two coffees, please.

22:59.780 --> 23:03.710
Watanabe, this is a cake shop.
Order some cake, will you?

23:03.710 --> 23:05.120
Got any recommendations?

23:05.120 --> 23:06.610
Sure do, and lots!

23:06.610 --> 23:09.880
If you want a seasonal cake, try the
strawberry soufflé and the sakura roll cake.

23:09.880 --> 23:13.990
And there's the new matcha mille-feuille. I'm proud of the greek yogurt mousse!

23:13.990 --> 23:14.920
I'll have that, then.

23:14.920 --> 23:17.140
Honda, aren't you putting out too many new cakes?

23:17.140 --> 23:18.760
I have fun making them.

23:18.760 --> 23:21.000
It's so fun, I don't have time to lose weight!

23:21.000 --> 23:24.100
If only there were 48 hours in a day.

23:24.100 --> 23:25.980
Then I'd get to make even more.

23:25.980 --> 23:28.310
Must be nice to do what you like for a—

23:28.840 --> 23:30.680
Please enjoy your stay.

23:31.300 --> 23:35.550
Watanabe, is it good news or bad news?

23:35.550 --> 23:37.360
Depends on how you view it.

23:37.360 --> 23:38.460
Huh?

23:40.830 --> 23:44.680
What do you think of the current state of Musani? As an anime studio.

23:44.680 --> 23:47.420
I think it was more or less inevitable.

23:47.420 --> 23:50.790
After the Time Hippo troubles,
we got no work, so the staff left.

23:50.790 --> 23:54.590
With no staff, we couldn't accept new work. It's a vicious cycle.

23:54.590 --> 23:57.030
The Time Hippo troubles, huh...

23:57.030 --> 23:58.480
And you?

23:58.480 --> 23:59.880
I don't like how it turned out.

23:59.880 --> 24:02.920
No, I mean, haven't you thought of quitting?

24:02.920 --> 24:05.210
Quit? My job? Or the company?

24:05.210 --> 24:07.570
Well, either one.

24:07.570 --> 24:10.720
No, I guess I'm mostly talking about the company.

24:10.720 --> 24:13.630
Watanabe! Are you closing up Musani?!

24:12.720 --> 24:15.540
Huh? What's that? Did you say galette quiche brioche?

24:15.540 --> 24:17.040
No, I didn't.

24:17.040 --> 24:19.360
You're making a face like you're out of ideas.

24:19.360 --> 24:20.870
No, we're not.

24:20.870 --> 24:21.730
Really?

24:22.000 --> 24:26.220
Oh, for that mousse, I tried using lychee liqueur for flavoring. What'cha think?

24:26.220 --> 24:27.550
I haven't tried it yet.

24:27.550 --> 24:31.590
Oh, really? Come on, hurry up and taste it.

24:31.590 --> 24:35.140
What is it? Just get to the point, Watanabe.

24:36.130 --> 24:38.000
Say, just for the sake of argument,

24:38.000 --> 24:42.250
that you had a chance to do a film at the current Musani. What would you do?

24:43.580 --> 24:45.080
A film?

24:45.080 --> 24:47.050
You mean as in a feature film?

24:47.050 --> 24:49.050
What other kind of film would I be talking about?

24:49.050 --> 24:50.210
As assistants?

24:51.070 --> 24:52.620
As the lead studio?

24:52.620 --> 24:55.430
Say you were making a film as the lead studio.

25:10.550 --> 25:12.110
I'll be back this Friday.

25:12.110 --> 25:14.150
All right! See you then!

25:15.160 --> 25:17.530
Say you were making... this.

25:27.930 --> 25:29.360
There you have it.

25:27.930 --> 25:29.360
The premiere date...

25:30.710 --> 25:33.990
It's almost May 2019, you know.

25:33.990 --> 25:34.760
I know.

25:34.760 --> 25:36.640
We only have ten months!

25:36.640 --> 25:37.510
I know.

25:37.510 --> 25:41.340
An original feature film?
Won't that take at least two years?

25:41.340 --> 25:41.970
Well...

25:42.520 --> 25:44.600
Want to see an old teaser?

25:44.600 --> 25:45.980
An old one?

25:54.070 --> 25:56.400
PRODUCTION IS CRUISING ALONG!

25:54.070 --> 25:56.400
PREMIERES FEBRUARY 2020

25:54.900 --> 25:54.940
Aerial Amphibious Assault Ship

26:25.260 --> 26:27.270
Hey, Miyamori!

26:28.530 --> 26:30.250
Takanashi? What are you doing here?

26:30.250 --> 26:31.130
You free?

26:31.130 --> 26:35.210
I am not. I'm picking up material at Zabo and then visiting President Marukawa.

26:33.530 --> 26:35.680
Oh hey, we're headed the same way!

26:35.680 --> 26:37.400
Give me a ride to Attacs.

26:37.400 --> 26:38.340
Why should I?

26:38.340 --> 26:39.880
C'mon, just do it.

26:39.880 --> 26:42.770
Hey! I'm telling Okitsu on you!

26:42.770 --> 26:43.790
She doesn't scare me!

26:43.790 --> 26:45.500
I'll sic Yano on you.

26:46.300 --> 26:49.250
She's busy with her family now anyway.
Just drive already!

26:52.390 --> 26:56.590
Hey, I did this. Takes me back.

26:57.670 --> 26:59.190
So what'cha up to nowadays, Miyamori?

26:59.190 --> 27:01.470
What do you think? I'm making anime.

27:01.470 --> 27:02.810
I'm more curious about you.

27:02.810 --> 27:05.210
Yeah, you better believe I'm making anime!

27:05.210 --> 27:07.160
Cretaceous Angels: Fkooin and Nihonon.

27:07.160 --> 27:10.850
Except I heard you're having a spat with Director Mijikai right now.

27:10.850 --> 27:12.630
I wouldn't call that a spat.

27:12.630 --> 27:15.360
A genius and a prodigy. It's a battle of talents!

27:15.360 --> 27:17.650
And we did make up in the end.

27:17.650 --> 27:18.860
Oh, pull over.

27:18.860 --> 27:20.250
Stop at the bus stop.

27:20.250 --> 27:21.300
What?!

27:22.450 --> 27:22.490
Musashino Animation

27:22.920 --> 27:26.940
Dai, get in! Miyamori's giving us a ride!

27:26.940 --> 27:28.470
Seriously?

27:28.470 --> 27:30.210
Well, I guess I'll take her up on that.

27:30.670 --> 27:33.120
Are you doing work for Attacs now?

27:33.120 --> 27:34.210
Nope, not us.

27:34.210 --> 27:35.890
We're about to <i>get</i> some.

27:35.890 --> 27:37.750
I thought you got an offer.

27:37.750 --> 27:41.360
No, we're going to propose a project to an acquaintance there.

27:41.360 --> 27:42.590
You're not going to a producer?

27:43.110 --> 27:45.340
Plebs like us?

27:45.340 --> 27:48.490
You really think a producer would give us the time of day?

27:48.490 --> 27:50.800
It's faster to go through a studio.

27:50.800 --> 27:55.900
The big companies only care about making popular and safe stuff.

27:55.900 --> 27:59.530
Though part of it is that my projects are just too avant garde.

27:59.530 --> 28:02.170
Any company would rather play it safe.

28:02.170 --> 28:06.770
Not to mention, some supposedly safe IPs haven't been doing well lately.

28:06.770 --> 28:07.910
Yeah, I know what you mean.

28:07.910 --> 28:11.300
We wanna get their expectations up and then blow those out of the water!

28:11.300 --> 28:12.430
What kind of anime is it?

28:12.430 --> 28:13.820
Wanna hear? Don't steal it.

28:13.820 --> 28:15.080
As if.

28:15.080 --> 28:18.210
Which one do you want?
I like the ensemble cast sci-fi one.

28:18.210 --> 28:19.790
I've got around five with me today.

28:19.790 --> 28:20.590
Five?

28:20.590 --> 28:23.740
A space station which turns into a locked room that's out of this world!

28:23.740 --> 28:25.600
Then there's a sudden murder!

28:25.600 --> 28:28.970
Surreal dying messages!
Love and hate! The plot thickens!

28:28.970 --> 28:29.980
What'cha think?

28:29.980 --> 28:32.350
Are those all serious proposals?

28:32.350 --> 28:33.360
Wow, rude.

28:33.360 --> 28:35.460
A lot of them get rejected, though.

28:35.460 --> 28:37.330
In fact, all of them have so far.

28:37.330 --> 28:39.910
We're just ahead of our time is all.

28:39.910 --> 28:42.670
I've seen more people than I can count insist on that before giving up.

28:42.670 --> 28:44.590
I'm confident about these!

28:44.590 --> 28:46.770
Blood group A came first on this morning's horoscope.

28:46.770 --> 28:48.690
Oh, but your group B came last.

28:48.690 --> 28:50.450
That just evens out, then.

28:50.450 --> 28:52.710
Oh, this is perfect. We're getting off here.

28:52.710 --> 28:57.470
Well done, Miyamori. Feel free to brag about having given Tarou Takanashi a ride this day.

28:57.470 --> 28:58.340
Sure, whatever.

28:58.340 --> 29:03.980
And if you ever make it big,
I'll brag about having let <i>the</i> Miyamori give me a ride.

29:03.980 --> 29:05.660
Now <i>that</i> sounds more likely.

29:05.660 --> 29:07.780
Oh, I can't believe you!

29:07.780 --> 29:09.060
Let's get going.

29:10.020 --> 29:11.910
Thanks for the ride. You're a lifesaver.

29:11.910 --> 29:12.560
No problem.

29:12.870 --> 29:17.310
I hope... things turn out okay for Musani.

29:17.310 --> 29:18.890
Oh... Thanks.

29:18.890 --> 29:20.910
If you're bored, why not propose something?

29:20.910 --> 29:23.710
Making that Seven Lucky Warriors thing is your dream, right?

29:23.710 --> 29:24.450
Huh?

29:24.450 --> 29:28.120
I read it in an interview with Imai Midori on Petersburg.

29:28.120 --> 29:30.390
That's from way back in high school.

29:30.390 --> 29:33.770
There's a lot of annoying and irritating stuff on the way,

29:33.770 --> 29:37.840
but if you've got something you want to do, you gotta fight to get it.

29:37.840 --> 29:41.460
If you don't, you won't get anywhere, and you'll be stuck in the same place.

29:41.460 --> 29:43.790
Or at least that's what I think.

29:54.390 --> 29:57.270
As of today, we're halting production.

30:07.010 --> 30:08.160
Hello.

30:08.880 --> 30:11.620
Oh, hi there, Miyamori.

30:13.960 --> 30:15.450
Would you like something to eat?

30:19.720 --> 30:21.190
Curry, please.

30:23.670 --> 30:25.210
Here you are.

30:25.670 --> 30:27.030
Thank you.

30:54.950 --> 30:58.110
Is today's curry a bit on the spicy side?

30:59.830 --> 31:02.590
No, it's the same.

31:02.590 --> 31:05.620
It's the same curry that you always used to make for us.

31:05.620 --> 31:07.050
Do you want seconds?

31:07.910 --> 31:09.050
Yes, please!

31:09.050 --> 31:13.430
I was always worried that I wouldn't be able to make it like before.

31:13.430 --> 31:16.310
I couldn't bring myself to make it for a while, you see.

31:16.550 --> 31:17.820
I just couldn't.

31:19.680 --> 31:21.310
Halting production?

31:21.570 --> 31:23.210
You mean temporarily, right?

31:23.210 --> 31:26.320
No, completely halted. As in canceled for good.

31:26.320 --> 31:28.190
And it won't be aired, either.

31:28.190 --> 31:29.160
Why?!

31:29.160 --> 31:32.660
Apparently they hadn't run the project by Trap.

31:32.660 --> 31:37.090
After last month's leadership change,
they held an urgent planning meeting on the topic,

31:37.090 --> 31:39.410
but they said they can't finance this project.

31:39.410 --> 31:42.880
Musani's original anime,
meant to start airing in January,

31:42.880 --> 31:47.110
Time Hippopotamus, has officially been canceled.

31:47.110 --> 31:49.550
But it's already been animated up to episode eight.

31:49.550 --> 31:52.430
Stop all work on it. Tell the staff immediately.

31:52.430 --> 31:55.930
But I put my heart and soul into the storyboard for the epilogue of episode six!

31:55.930 --> 31:57.560
I'm sorry. You'll have another chance.

31:57.560 --> 32:00.890
Even if Trap won't sponsor it,
maybe there's another place that will take it?

32:00.890 --> 32:03.670
The original character designer was brought on by Trap,

32:03.670 --> 32:07.120
so it would be difficult to get him on board without them.

32:07.120 --> 32:10.580
There are both moral and rights issues involved.

32:11.150 --> 32:14.530
I'll compile a list of parties that we've contracted and how much we owe.

32:16.420 --> 32:17.330
Goddammit!

32:21.190 --> 32:22.360
Director...

32:27.180 --> 32:28.880
Don't worry about me.

32:28.880 --> 32:30.800
So it got canceled, what can you do?

32:31.650 --> 32:35.980
But you know, everyone put so much effort into it, you know?

32:35.980 --> 32:40.560
The episode directors, the artists, the animators,
the coloring staff, the filming staff, all of them.

32:40.560 --> 32:43.310
We had something special going.

32:43.310 --> 32:46.130
Something real special.

32:47.180 --> 32:49.570
Tristan, Tategami, Issui...

32:50.000 --> 32:52.990
Now what will become of all of them?

32:52.990 --> 32:57.890
And just as they'd finally reunited with Claudel,
and their adventure was just getting started...

33:05.450 --> 33:06.420
I'm sorry...

33:06.810 --> 33:09.000
We'd been working with the producer for a long time,

33:09.000 --> 33:13.390
and I guess we got a bit too comfortable after our success with Two Piece.

33:14.100 --> 33:17.500
Things stayed on track better than anything we'd ever done at Musani.

33:17.500 --> 33:20.600
We had two complete episodes a whole three months before the airing.

33:21.370 --> 33:23.560
But it all ended up going to waste.

33:23.560 --> 33:28.330
We started making it before any contracts were signed or the budget had been deposited.

33:28.330 --> 33:29.770
It's all my fault.

33:29.770 --> 33:33.030
No, you worked harder than any of us, President!

33:33.030 --> 33:35.550
We only avoided bankruptcy thanks to you.

33:35.550 --> 33:38.280
But we ended up back at square one.

33:38.280 --> 33:42.060
We may be flying a bit low right now,
but we'll make a comeback one day!

33:42.060 --> 33:43.180
Are you sure?

33:43.180 --> 33:44.690
Musani will soar again!

33:45.400 --> 33:46.790
I see.

33:47.760 --> 33:51.170
Though it would be even better if you came back.

33:51.170 --> 33:53.030
Now that I can't do.

33:54.020 --> 33:58.650
The condition was that I took responsibility and stepped down.

33:58.650 --> 34:02.240
That was the best decision,
practically and symbolically.

34:02.240 --> 34:06.920
Besides, you'll be forging ahead down new paths, making new anime.

34:06.920 --> 34:09.200
That's what you have to do.

34:09.200 --> 34:10.820
New anime...

34:10.820 --> 34:14.470
Miyamori, why do you make anime?

34:15.320 --> 34:21.080
Well... Because I love anime,
and I love the people who make anime...

34:22.360 --> 34:23.470
And?

34:25.940 --> 34:29.570
Doing something because you love it is wonderful.

34:29.570 --> 34:31.810
But that's not enough.

34:31.810 --> 34:36.340
What do you want to make,
and what do you want to achieve with it?

34:36.340 --> 34:39.960
If you don't know that, sooner or later you'll burn out.

34:41.350 --> 34:46.480
I want you all to have pride and confidence in the work you do.

34:46.480 --> 34:49.530
To make something filled with passion, love, ambition.

34:49.530 --> 34:54.230
Anime that makes the creator grow and the audience happy.

34:54.230 --> 34:58.140
You young ones will explore untrodden ground,

34:58.140 --> 35:03.620
and by doing so, you'll be a guiding light for even younger ones still.

35:03.620 --> 35:06.760
That's what I expect of you.

35:07.610 --> 35:09.370
A guiding light...

35:09.370 --> 35:10.630
That's right.

35:10.630 --> 35:14.710
You don't have time to stand still and worry about the past.

35:14.710 --> 35:18.230
Just focus on moving forward.

35:39.210 --> 35:42.020
For starters, for starters

35:44.720 --> 35:50.410
For starters, let's get this started

35:50.410 --> 35:53.290
Let's give it a go, let's give it a go

35:56.490 --> 36:01.720
I'm a little bit scared, but let's give it a go

36:02.090 --> 36:03.440
You'll give it a go?

36:03.440 --> 36:04.610
Do you mean it?

36:04.610 --> 36:05.960
For real?

36:07.280 --> 36:09.810
I'm serious, and I mean it

36:09.810 --> 36:12.060
It'll be fine

36:12.060 --> 36:13.020
A baseless...

36:13.020 --> 36:14.080
..."it'll be fine"...

36:14.080 --> 36:16.080
...isn't fine at all.

36:17.320 --> 36:20.120
I'm not forcing myself or going with the flow

36:20.120 --> 36:23.040
It'll be fine

36:25.640 --> 36:27.970
For starters, for starters

36:27.970 --> 36:30.230
For starters

36:30.230 --> 36:32.600
Let's give it a go, let's give it a go

36:32.600 --> 36:34.880
Let's give it a go

36:34.880 --> 36:39.760
It doesn't have much weight, but let it roll

36:39.760 --> 36:44.010
Spin the flywheel, let it roll

36:44.010 --> 36:46.560
If you spin it, it should roll

36:46.560 --> 36:49.010
Round and round

36:49.010 --> 36:51.640
As far as it can, round and round

36:51.640 --> 36:53.350
Round and round

36:53.350 --> 36:55.810
If you don't spin it, nothing will happen

36:55.810 --> 36:57.980
It'll be over before you start

36:57.980 --> 37:00.880
First you have to make it roll

37:00.880 --> 37:02.570
Round and round

37:02.570 --> 37:05.140
Round round and round, round round and round

37:05.140 --> 37:09.660
Round round and round, it grows bigger and bigger

37:09.660 --> 37:12.000
Round round and round

37:12.000 --> 37:14.290
Round round and round, round round and round

37:14.290 --> 37:16.630
Round round and round, round round and round

37:16.630 --> 37:19.070
Round, round, round

37:19.070 --> 37:21.780
Round round and round

37:23.870 --> 37:25.390
Hey! Get a grip!

37:25.390 --> 37:26.990
Look up at the sky

37:26.990 --> 37:29.850
Rub the arch of your foot

37:29.850 --> 37:32.850
Don't be so indecisive and stop blubbering

37:32.860 --> 37:33.960
Your fist isn't some weapon

37:33.460 --> 37:33.960
Your

37:33.460 --> 37:33.960
fist

37:33.460 --> 37:33.960
isn't

37:33.960 --> 37:36.190
Your fist isn't some weapon

37:36.190 --> 37:38.940
Tuck that lower lip back in

37:38.940 --> 37:40.440
Stop whining

37:40.440 --> 37:42.200
Don't be so drab

37:42.200 --> 37:46.360
I know, but I'm a loser, so there's no point

37:46.360 --> 37:47.990
Don't say that!

37:48.000 --> 37:50.620
It doesn't matter if you win or lose!

37:50.620 --> 37:53.270
And reception, um, well... Doesn't matter!

37:53.270 --> 37:53.700
And

37:53.270 --> 37:53.700
reception,

37:53.270 --> 37:53.700
um,

37:53.270 --> 37:53.700
well...

37:53.270 --> 37:53.700
Doesn't

37:53.270 --> 37:53.700
matter!

37:53.710 --> 37:56.640
Stop shivering and wandering aimlessly

37:56.640 --> 37:59.960
Rub your hands together to warm up

37:59.970 --> 38:04.050
Fill in the highlights in your eyes

38:04.050 --> 38:05.760
And try glaring a bit

38:05.760 --> 38:08.430
Dump all your feelings into it

38:08.430 --> 38:13.440
And try making some animation

38:28.580 --> 38:30.240
One cute and cool

38:30.250 --> 38:32.290
Or ugly yet lovable

38:32.290 --> 38:36.290
One that's nerve-racking or edgy

38:36.300 --> 38:41.250
Let's make some anime

38:43.690 --> 38:47.260
Let's make some, let's make some

38:47.270 --> 38:51.060
Let's make some anime

38:51.060 --> 38:54.850
Let's make one, let's make one

38:54.850 --> 38:58.570
Let's make an anime film

38:58.570 --> 39:02.320
Where surging passion is calmly deflected

39:02.320 --> 39:06.320
An exciting one that leaves an impression

39:06.320 --> 39:09.940
Let's make some anime

39:09.940 --> 39:12.980
The Andes are an awesome place

39:12.980 --> 39:18.600
So let's make some animation

39:22.930 --> 39:24.600
Let's make some, let's make some

39:28.430 --> 39:30.310
Animation

40:05.220 --> 40:08.610
Nabe... Miyamori...
Thank you so much for coming.

40:08.610 --> 40:10.740
You simply showing up makes me so happy.

40:10.740 --> 40:12.440
Miyamori, I'm sorry about the other day.

40:12.440 --> 40:13.970
Oh, don't worry about it.

40:13.970 --> 40:16.850
Also, I'm sorry for what's coming too.

40:16.850 --> 40:17.390
Huh?

40:17.390 --> 40:18.750
I'll have the coffee blend.

40:18.750 --> 40:20.350
I'll have the same.

40:20.350 --> 40:22.920
Excuse me! Could we make an order?

40:22.920 --> 40:25.820
Their sandwich platter and cheesecake are really good.

40:25.820 --> 40:27.510
Want some? I'll have some.

40:27.510 --> 40:28.630
Oh, no, I'm good.

40:28.630 --> 40:31.240
Really? What a shame.

40:32.200 --> 40:32.280
GePeU!

40:41.290 --> 40:41.910
And the rest?!

40:42.180 --> 40:43.750
That's all of it.

40:47.130 --> 40:49.090
You lied to me!

40:49.090 --> 40:49.220
You lied to me!

40:49.670 --> 40:51.830
Hold on there, Katsuragi.

40:51.830 --> 40:53.190
That's a nasty accusation.

40:53.190 --> 40:56.970
Well, who's the one who said "yeah, yeah, we're
working on it" when you weren't doing a damn thing?!

40:56.970 --> 40:57.760
Get the director!

40:57.760 --> 41:00.760
The director's the one who said he'd go straight to storyboards without a writer!

41:00.760 --> 41:02.160
How did it end up like this?!

41:02.160 --> 41:04.300
Well, he's busy, you know.

41:04.300 --> 41:07.110
He can't really afford to spend all his time on this.

41:07.110 --> 41:10.880
You said we'd discuss it if there was a problem with the schedule!

41:10.880 --> 41:13.170
All I heard was "it's fine," "we're on track"!

41:12.210 --> 41:14.780
Try putting yourself in our shoes.

41:14.780 --> 41:18.090
We were being considerate by not making you worry about it being late.

41:18.090 --> 41:20.890
You can take that consideration and shove it!
I want the storyboards!

41:20.890 --> 41:23.250
Now, now, it's not like we didn't <i>want</i> to make it.

41:23.250 --> 41:26.430
You had two years!
How can you even begin to claim that?!

41:26.430 --> 41:28.740
I wasn't planning on bringing it up at this point...

41:28.740 --> 41:31.490
But you know your previous producer, Mikebuchi?

41:31.490 --> 41:33.980
He's horrible at estimating a budget.

41:33.980 --> 41:37.040
You can't make a movie like SIVA on that budget.

41:38.720 --> 41:41.940
You... You... I-In that case...

41:41.010 --> 41:43.060
Heya, sure, got it.

41:43.060 --> 41:46.060
I'll be right there. Yup. See ya.

41:46.060 --> 41:48.060
I'm terribly sorry, Katsuragi.

41:48.060 --> 41:51.060
I've got a meeting after this,
so I'm afraid we'll have to leave it there.

41:51.740 --> 41:55.780
The deal was that you'd spend two years on it and have it ready one year before the premiere!

41:55.780 --> 41:57.920
Come on, just wait another month.

41:57.920 --> 42:02.010
Another month or two doesn't make much of a difference, right?

42:01.030 --> 42:03.750
It absolutely does!

42:02.680 --> 42:03.750
Although...

42:03.750 --> 42:07.350
We might be able to figure something out if you give us a bigger budget.

42:07.350 --> 42:09.920
I hope you won't let us down.

42:09.920 --> 42:13.730
God, that must have been what boiling with rage is like!

42:13.730 --> 42:14.480
I see...

42:14.480 --> 42:16.110
Thank you so much, Miyamori.

42:16.110 --> 42:19.070
If you hadn't cheered me up back then,
who knows what would have happened.

42:19.070 --> 42:21.060
When did I cheer you up?

42:21.060 --> 42:22.590
Thank God for Nabe...

42:22.590 --> 42:25.930
No, thank God for you, Miyamori. Really.

42:26.390 --> 42:28.750
I took the project out of GePeU's hands,

42:28.750 --> 42:31.080
so I'm sure it'll be hard,
but do your best to finish the movie.

42:31.080 --> 42:32.010
Yes, sure.

42:32.010 --> 42:34.520
We'll make that GePeU president cry!

42:34.520 --> 42:36.580
We'll make something that takes the world by storm!

42:36.580 --> 42:36.880
Sure.

42:36.880 --> 42:39.820
And then he'll wish that he'd actually... Huh?

42:40.730 --> 42:41.530
Sure.

42:42.540 --> 42:44.870
Did you hear that, Nabe?! She said yes!

42:44.870 --> 42:46.960
Miyamori said Y-E-S!

42:46.960 --> 42:50.060
What a relief. Now I can die happy.

42:50.060 --> 42:51.680
Oh, thank you.

42:54.300 --> 42:56.470
Oh, this is Miyai.

42:56.470 --> 43:00.260
She'll be taking over from the
previous producer, Mikebuchi.

43:00.260 --> 43:03.430
I'm Miyai. It's a pleasure to make your acquaintance.

43:03.430 --> 43:04.910
Here to clean up his mess?

43:04.910 --> 43:05.680
More or less.

43:05.680 --> 43:08.350
Mikebuchi resigned, you see.

43:08.350 --> 43:12.540
Well, us old folk will take care of the boring stuff.

43:12.540 --> 43:15.820
So I guess the youngsters are relieved for the day.

43:16.140 --> 43:18.600
I'd like to confirm a few things.

43:18.600 --> 43:19.320
Sure.

43:19.320 --> 43:21.220
Will we be the lead studio?

43:21.220 --> 43:21.820
Indeed.

43:21.820 --> 43:25.710
Are the production committee okay with that?

43:25.710 --> 43:26.330
Quite.

43:26.330 --> 43:27.820
It's a complete original?

43:27.820 --> 43:28.330
Yes.

43:28.330 --> 43:29.370
And the title?

43:29.370 --> 43:31.460
Aerial Amphibious Assault Ship SIVA.

43:31.700 --> 43:32.600
Can we change it?

43:32.600 --> 43:34.340
It's already been announced, I'm afraid.

43:34.340 --> 43:35.240
How long?

43:35.240 --> 43:36.590
Ninety minutes, give or take.

43:36.590 --> 43:37.580
And the premiere date?

43:37.580 --> 43:39.300
February 2020.

43:39.300 --> 43:40.190
The staff?

43:40.190 --> 43:42.040
We'll leave that to you at Musani.

43:42.040 --> 43:42.800
Understood.

43:43.090 --> 43:44.780
Well, with that settled...

43:44.780 --> 43:45.810
With that settled...

43:46.530 --> 43:48.530
How would you like to go for a light meal?

43:48.530 --> 43:49.810
Sure. A light one.

43:50.450 --> 43:51.810
And I'm like, "just die"!

43:53.620 --> 43:57.410
Who the hell abandons their own project to go to some other company?

43:57.410 --> 43:58.250
Die!

43:58.250 --> 44:00.610
Corporate politics must be rough.

44:00.610 --> 44:03.060
Yes! They really are!

44:03.060 --> 44:04.990
And it's all so half-assed there! It sucks!

44:06.910 --> 44:09.310
I get you. I so get you, Miyai.

44:09.310 --> 44:12.940
Who do they think they are, making me mop up after their failure? Idiots! To hell with them!

44:12.940 --> 44:15.420
Failure! Utter defeat! Huge upset!

44:15.420 --> 44:17.420
That's right! An upset!

44:17.640 --> 44:19.820
Ninth inning, two outs, ten runs behind.

44:19.820 --> 44:22.880
Second half, two minutes of stoppage time,
three goals behind.

44:22.880 --> 44:24.480
And then victory!

44:24.480 --> 44:25.680
Victory!

44:25.800 --> 44:29.430
9 and a Half Months Until Premiere

44:25.950 --> 44:27.530
We'll show 'em what we can do!

44:27.530 --> 44:28.310
Let's do it!

44:28.310 --> 44:29.430
Yeah!

44:37.320 --> 44:38.570
Good morning.

44:38.570 --> 44:40.370
Good morning.

44:41.300 --> 44:44.070
We have a major announcement to make.

44:44.070 --> 44:48.830
Musashino Animation will be making a feature length film.

44:51.390 --> 44:53.920
Aerial Amphibious Assault Ship SIVA?

44:53.920 --> 44:55.420
What about the script and storyboards?

44:55.420 --> 44:56.570
Not done yet.

44:56.570 --> 44:57.710
Figured.

44:57.710 --> 44:59.230
Could this be a sci-fi movie?

44:57.710 --> 45:01.340
Sagura Yoshiki
Filming Director

44:59.230 --> 45:01.340
Isn't that pretty obvious?

45:01.690 --> 45:03.590
What should we decide on first?

45:03.590 --> 45:06.090
I mean, all we have to go on is the title.

45:06.090 --> 45:07.740
The major themes, to start off.

45:07.740 --> 45:11.000
Though I guess it's going to end up a battle anime, or an action anime.

45:11.000 --> 45:13.370
Is it a tearjerker? Comedic? Philosophical?

45:13.370 --> 45:15.980
Whatever the case, the sci-fi part is set in stone.

45:15.980 --> 45:20.630
Does the "aerial" part of "Aerial Amphibious Assault Ship SIVA" mean space?

45:20.630 --> 45:21.990
Or is it just flying in the air?

45:21.990 --> 45:24.620
And is SIVA the name of the ship?

45:24.620 --> 45:27.520
Or the name of an operation? An acronym?

45:27.520 --> 45:30.010
Or maybe a god? Or an unconscious collective entity?

45:30.010 --> 45:30.790
Um...

45:30.790 --> 45:35.170
Isn't what we need most right now
time and a general plot?

45:35.640 --> 45:37.920
I have an idea as far as that goes.

45:39.090 --> 45:43.550
Maybe we can make use of some of the material from our previous production, Time Hippopotamus?

45:44.470 --> 45:45.300
Time Hippo?

45:45.550 --> 45:50.080
That was a time travel anime, but the protagonist was a boy from the near future.

45:50.080 --> 45:53.430
I'm not saying to make the exact same thing all over again.

45:53.430 --> 45:57.240
We have so much we didn't do,
and couldn't even if we'd wanted to.

45:57.240 --> 45:59.190
I feel like we can pull it off now!

45:59.440 --> 46:01.440
I want to give it a go!

46:01.440 --> 46:03.740
Which means the director would be...

46:04.160 --> 46:05.880
We don't have much time,

46:05.880 --> 46:09.880
but I think this is a great opportunity to make up for last time, for both you and Musani.

46:09.880 --> 46:14.070
I don't think it's good to do something in such a backward-looking way.

46:14.070 --> 46:15.570
I'm sorry.

46:15.570 --> 46:20.200
I would love to see you create a movie for the ages. In a forward-thinking way.

46:20.850 --> 46:26.410
The more hours you put in and the harder you work, the emptier you feel.

46:26.410 --> 46:27.430
Huh?

46:27.430 --> 46:30.140
If you just feel empty, there's no point in doing it.

46:30.140 --> 46:33.310
And if there's no point, you don't have to do it.

46:33.310 --> 46:35.790
What about your living expenses?

46:35.790 --> 46:37.690
Good question. No idea.

46:37.690 --> 46:40.380
Right now I don't care what happens.

46:40.380 --> 46:41.570
What? No!

46:41.570 --> 46:44.530
It's been like this my whole life.

46:45.100 --> 46:48.530
As soon as I think things are going well, I plunge right to the bottom.

46:48.530 --> 46:50.660
It doesn't matter how hard I fight.

46:50.660 --> 46:51.880
You can't give up!

46:51.880 --> 46:53.970
I <i>have</i> to give up.

46:53.970 --> 46:56.300
I may have gotten ahead of myself the first time.

46:56.300 --> 46:59.400
But I didn't do anything wrong the second time around.

46:59.400 --> 47:01.330
Then let's give it another go!

47:01.330 --> 47:03.460
No. I'm afraid I'll just fail again.

47:03.460 --> 47:04.420
No you won't.

47:04.420 --> 47:08.890
If we panic and try to make it at top speed while going "just you see," we'll definitely fail,

47:08.890 --> 47:10.930
and the next time I fail, it's all over!

47:10.930 --> 47:12.930
You won't fail! Let's do all we can!

47:12.930 --> 47:13.780
I don't like the title.

47:13.780 --> 47:16.140
We can... not change it.

47:16.500 --> 47:17.900
But why not?

47:17.900 --> 47:22.200
Reminds me of my Shiba Inu, Seira.
I loved her, but my wife took her with her.

47:22.200 --> 47:25.350
I named her after the sei in Seiichi and the ra in Sakura.

47:25.350 --> 47:26.380
Seira!

47:26.380 --> 47:28.510
I'm sure Seira is doing just fine!

47:28.510 --> 47:29.990
I know that!

47:29.990 --> 47:32.310
I know, but what difference does it make if I can't see her?

47:32.310 --> 47:35.970
If I don't want to do it, I don't want to!

47:35.970 --> 47:36.830
Wait!

47:36.830 --> 47:37.410
I refuse!

47:41.620 --> 47:43.040
I'm sorr— huh?

47:43.040 --> 47:44.600
Honda?

47:44.600 --> 47:45.800
Director?!

47:45.800 --> 47:48.290
You're the only person for the job!

47:48.290 --> 47:50.300
I bet you're saying that to everyone.

47:50.300 --> 47:50.930
Yep.

47:50.930 --> 47:51.440
See!

47:51.440 --> 47:55.360
But you're the only one I've spoken to.

47:55.810 --> 47:57.270
Oh! Mont Blancs!

47:57.270 --> 47:58.380
Not so fast.

47:59.060 --> 48:01.920
The name Mont Blanc comes from the tallest mountain in Europe.

48:01.920 --> 48:07.600
Those who don't try are not worthy of a dessert bearing its proud name.

48:07.600 --> 48:08.190
What?!

48:08.190 --> 48:10.510
What's with that slovenly stomach of yours?

48:10.510 --> 48:12.070
Well, that goes for you too...

48:12.070 --> 48:13.610
I'm an athletic fatso.

48:13.610 --> 48:15.300
And I can make cakes too.

48:15.300 --> 48:16.490
What can you do?!

48:16.490 --> 48:17.180
I...

48:17.180 --> 48:18.710
You're just a fatso!

48:18.710 --> 48:19.500
I'm...

48:19.500 --> 48:20.570
He's a director fatso!

48:20.570 --> 48:21.810
You called me a fatso!

48:21.810 --> 48:24.050
Let's climb this mountain, Director!

48:24.050 --> 48:26.500
You can't just stand still and worry about the past.

48:26.500 --> 48:28.090
You have to move on!

48:28.380 --> 48:30.550
Or so the old president said.

48:30.550 --> 48:32.330
Marukawa said that?

48:32.330 --> 48:33.180
He did.

48:35.870 --> 48:37.560
Okay, fine.

48:37.950 --> 48:38.810
Great.

48:44.090 --> 48:47.440
I-It's not like I accepted it for these Mont Blancs or anything!

48:47.440 --> 48:48.290
We know.

48:48.290 --> 48:53.030
If Maitake's on board I'll do it,
but I don't think he will be.

48:53.030 --> 48:54.000
I'm on board.

48:54.530 --> 48:55.070
What?!

48:55.070 --> 48:56.030
Why?!

48:56.030 --> 49:00.540
Why do you think? The once-dead Time Hippo is about to be reborn and see the light of day.

49:00.540 --> 49:02.540
I can't think of a reason to decline.

49:02.540 --> 49:04.100
Oh, it's you next.

49:04.100 --> 49:06.080
Oh, uh... Right.

49:06.080 --> 49:08.300
Do we still have the old data?

49:11.300 --> 49:14.930
I have the data up to the second pass of episode 11 right here.

49:14.930 --> 49:16.180
It's got the image data too.

49:16.180 --> 49:18.450
Oh, thank you. You're a lifesaver.

49:21.180 --> 49:23.690
Oh right, this is where we stopped.

49:24.070 --> 49:28.350
Issui is wounded right at the end and loses consciousness.

49:28.350 --> 49:32.020
How was I planning on wrapping this up in two episodes again?

49:42.160 --> 49:44.300
I'll read it through from the start.

49:44.300 --> 49:46.950
I'll decide what to use and how...

49:49.380 --> 49:50.880
once we get started.

50:01.410 --> 50:02.640
Director!

50:03.170 --> 50:04.560
Are you here for that? For SIVA—

50:04.560 --> 50:06.770
I have made my shameful return!

50:06.770 --> 50:08.620
Please, let me help you!

50:08.620 --> 50:09.360
Really?

50:09.360 --> 50:14.240
Yeah. Too bad we won't see the return of the Musani triumvirate.

50:14.240 --> 50:16.280
Ah, you mean Yamada.

50:16.280 --> 50:20.240
He finally got to be a virtuoso. I doubt he'd want to come back now.

50:20.240 --> 50:23.550
And I bet you're gonna leave me for new heights too, aren't you?

50:23.550 --> 50:24.870
Congratulations, you bastard.

50:24.870 --> 50:27.140
New heights? Where would I find those?

50:27.140 --> 50:29.330
Well, I'll just do what I can.

50:29.330 --> 50:32.050
Director, about the character designer and mechanical designer...

50:32.380 --> 50:35.500
I'd like to find someone to help out as soon as possible.

50:35.500 --> 50:38.680
Well, let's see... We're looking for friends to fight alongside...

50:39.950 --> 50:42.810
Personally I'd like to ask Endou to be the mechanical designer.

50:42.810 --> 50:44.770
If I can...

50:44.770 --> 50:48.020
He did Time Hippo together with Iguchi, after all.

50:48.020 --> 50:50.200
Are you able to get in contact with Endou?

50:50.200 --> 50:51.020
No...

50:51.020 --> 50:52.200
I see...

50:52.200 --> 50:55.780
He was more invested in the show than anyone.

50:56.080 --> 51:00.060
Yeah, I haven't heard from him in ages either.

51:00.060 --> 51:01.290
I see...

51:01.290 --> 51:04.990
I heard he's been going from place to place, failing to deliver work and starting fights.

51:04.990 --> 51:07.460
He probably hasn't been working much lately.

51:07.680 --> 51:10.830
We've tried to get ahold of him at Musani a few times...

51:10.830 --> 51:13.380
I really feel bad about what happened with Time Hippo.

51:13.380 --> 51:16.610
But who'd get driven to despair by that sort of thing?

51:17.340 --> 51:21.470
I guess guys are just more sensitive in that respect.

51:21.810 --> 51:24.100
Would you be interested in this project, Iguchi?

51:24.100 --> 51:25.430
I'll do it!

51:24.960 --> 51:26.380
Thank you so much!

51:25.430 --> 51:27.060
Or so I'd like to say.

51:27.380 --> 51:30.580
The schedule clashes perfectly with another project.

51:31.080 --> 51:34.320
I can probably help out with character design, but animation director, no chance.

51:34.320 --> 51:35.820
Are you okay with that?

51:36.750 --> 51:38.360
Of course! I'd love to have you on board!

51:38.360 --> 51:39.900
In that case, I'll do it.

51:39.900 --> 51:41.450
Thank you so much!

51:43.950 --> 51:46.030
I guess I'm a bit early...

51:47.030 --> 51:47.660
Huh?!

51:50.420 --> 51:52.270
No! This isn't what it seems!

51:52.270 --> 51:54.670
R-Right! Of course not!

51:54.670 --> 51:58.770
I have been informed of your request to have me as an animation director for a new film.

51:58.770 --> 52:02.850
However, I am not currently accepting any offers other than for key animation.

52:02.850 --> 52:04.560
Huh? How come?

52:04.560 --> 52:09.130
To me, an animator is someone who makes things move.

52:09.130 --> 52:11.440
I have to develop my ability to do so when I can,

52:11.750 --> 52:15.570
or I can see myself regretting it ten, twenty years down the line.

52:15.570 --> 52:17.380
So I want to devote myself to it.

52:17.380 --> 52:19.210
Twenty years down the line...

52:19.780 --> 52:22.590
It may not be much, but instead,

52:22.590 --> 52:24.950
could you perhaps let me participate as a key animator?

52:24.950 --> 52:28.320
I would love to assist with the first Musani anime in a while.

52:29.260 --> 52:30.830
Thank you so much!

52:30.830 --> 52:34.080
With that, we tentatively have the pre-credits sequence.

52:34.080 --> 52:37.110
Now I'd like to get the storyboarding started.

52:37.110 --> 52:38.230
I'll do my best.

52:38.230 --> 52:41.820
It's a bit late, but would it be possible to find material on natto?

52:41.820 --> 52:43.660
Like the origin and where it's eaten.

52:43.660 --> 52:45.470
Understood. I'll have it first thing tomorrow.

52:45.810 --> 52:47.390
A question for the director.

52:47.390 --> 52:49.630
In the first scene where they fight a giant octopus at sea,

52:49.630 --> 52:52.420
will the octopus be CG too,
along with the assault ship?

52:52.420 --> 52:54.990
Good question... Is CG even possible?

52:54.990 --> 52:57.940
We can change it if need be.
Could be a lobster or even a killer whale.

52:57.940 --> 53:00.140
Lobster... Sounds delicious...

53:00.140 --> 53:03.450
Won't it be hard to mix hard and soft elements?

53:03.450 --> 53:06.660
Well, if the octopus crushes the ship, exposing the internals,

53:06.660 --> 53:10.330
or if debris starts flying, we'd definitely need some extra time.

53:10.330 --> 53:12.340
Just the octopus, then.

53:12.340 --> 53:14.140
Got it. Better start gathering data.

53:14.140 --> 53:15.770
I'll collect video.

53:15.770 --> 53:17.380
Anything else?

53:18.470 --> 53:22.340
In that case, I'll end today's script meeting.

53:22.340 --> 53:26.410
Thank you for letting me join the team.
I look forward to working with you.

53:26.410 --> 53:27.850
We look forward to working with you.

53:27.850 --> 53:31.350
Also, it will be impossible for the director to handle all the storyboarding and directing alone,

53:31.350 --> 53:33.170
but I have three people in mind.

53:33.170 --> 53:35.230
You're okay with that, right, Director?

53:35.230 --> 53:37.030
I'm sorry for being slow!

53:37.030 --> 53:39.360
However, only Madoka has agreed so far.

53:39.360 --> 53:41.900
What about the ADs? I'd like at least three.

53:41.900 --> 53:44.740
I'm considering Segawa and...

53:44.740 --> 53:45.970
What about Endou?

53:45.970 --> 53:47.120
Not yet.

53:48.810 --> 53:51.740
Would you mind if I asked Yasuhara on board as an AD?

53:52.250 --> 53:55.280
She's been steadily advancing her career as an animation director,

53:55.280 --> 53:58.880
and knows both you and Iguchi,
so I think she'd be a good fit. Besides—

53:58.880 --> 54:00.440
Sure, why not?

54:00.440 --> 54:01.380
Really?

54:01.380 --> 54:02.130
Yeah.

54:02.570 --> 54:05.990
I'll get the equipment set up properly by the start of next week.

54:05.990 --> 54:08.780
I'm sorry for making you wait.

54:08.780 --> 54:12.890
Don't worry, I need to go get my stuff from Grape anyway.

54:12.890 --> 54:14.980
Is Segawa already on board as an AD?

54:14.980 --> 54:17.800
We just need to go over the schedule in detail.

54:18.650 --> 54:19.650
Got it.

54:19.650 --> 54:21.830
All right! Thank you for helping out!

54:34.020 --> 54:35.760
Thank you, come again.

54:35.760 --> 54:36.790
Sorry to keep you waiting.

54:36.790 --> 54:38.200
Welcome.

54:41.660 --> 54:43.800
It's a common story, isn't it?

54:43.800 --> 54:47.980
What you want to do, what you can do,
and what you're forced to do being different.

54:47.980 --> 54:49.240
I suppose so...

54:49.240 --> 54:50.430
So, what were you saying?

54:50.430 --> 54:52.960
I'm happy to be receiving work,

54:52.960 --> 54:56.020
and if I work hard now,
I'm sure someone will recognize it.

54:56.020 --> 54:57.810
I think, at least.

54:57.810 --> 55:00.670
But at the same time, I feel like I need to take some initiative.

55:00.670 --> 55:02.980
I'm worried I'm just going with the flow.

55:04.910 --> 55:08.310
Sakaki, you'll never believe my husband!

55:08.310 --> 55:11.220
When our child is crying, he never even thinks to hold him.

55:11.220 --> 55:13.620
Meanwhile, my headache is so bad I can't do anything!

55:13.620 --> 55:18.050
When your child cries, most people would wonder if he's hungry or needs his diapers changed, right?

55:18.050 --> 55:20.580
I got so angry I haven't spoken to him all day!

55:20.580 --> 55:23.170
And then he asks, "Where's my lunch?" Can you believe it?

55:24.310 --> 55:26.160
Why don't you just ask him?

55:26.160 --> 55:29.450
"I'll feed him, so could you hold him?"

55:29.450 --> 55:32.930
"My head hurts, so would you mind doing this?"

55:32.930 --> 55:35.930
But what if he says no?

55:35.930 --> 55:38.200
Worry about that after you've asked.

55:38.200 --> 55:39.840
First you need to explain what you need.

55:42.400 --> 55:43.400
Pretty much.

55:43.960 --> 55:47.150
Agencies and voice actors are like a couple in a way.

55:47.150 --> 55:50.470
You have to think of them as an inconsiderate husband.

55:50.470 --> 55:51.440
Right...

55:51.440 --> 55:56.930
However, unlike with couples, you have to take responsibility for your decisions.

55:56.930 --> 55:58.830
Whether you fail or succeed.

55:59.410 --> 56:02.790
If you're confident and determined enough, then do it.

56:03.310 --> 56:05.590
Confidence and determination...

56:17.270 --> 56:17.390
Shimoyanagi

56:17.270 --> 56:17.390
Incoming Call

56:35.720 --> 56:39.750
I see you still have a bad habit of waiting for a moment before using Spin of Earth.

56:40.320 --> 56:44.130
Well, your combos used to be a lot sharper than this.

56:45.500 --> 56:46.980
Why won't you pick up your phone?

56:46.980 --> 56:48.270
Because I don't want to.

56:48.270 --> 56:49.800
And why don't you want to?

56:49.800 --> 56:51.290
Why do I have to have a reason?

56:51.290 --> 56:53.180
I don't want to pick it up, so I don't.

56:53.180 --> 56:54.580
You're running away.

56:53.860 --> 56:54.580
I am not.

56:54.580 --> 56:56.140
You clearly are.

56:56.140 --> 56:57.570
So what are you doing here, Segawa?

56:57.570 --> 56:58.240
Nothing much.

56:58.240 --> 56:59.680
You're bothering me, you know!

57:00.000 --> 57:03.190
It's not like I need your permission to be here.

57:03.190 --> 57:05.500
I suppose I don't have a reason to stay, then.

57:05.500 --> 57:08.690
And you get grumpy quickly just like before too.

57:08.690 --> 57:10.780
You sound like my mother. Quit it.

57:10.780 --> 57:12.570
Then stop worrying everyone.

57:12.570 --> 57:14.990
And stop acting the all-knowing senior. It's annoying.

57:14.990 --> 57:18.450
Then stop causing problems and do some actual work.

57:18.450 --> 57:22.660
Letting Mayumi do all the work when you have loans... Aren't you ashamed?

57:23.210 --> 57:25.210
Stop getting up in other people's business!

57:25.210 --> 57:28.390
Excuse me?! I'd say I'm going easy on you if anything!

57:28.390 --> 57:30.670
You have no right to judge how I lead my life!

57:30.670 --> 57:33.340
Your life?! Can you really say you're living right now?

57:33.340 --> 57:36.610
What good is going to come from refusing to let go of old baggage?

57:36.610 --> 57:38.290
You just end up rotting away!

57:38.290 --> 57:39.560
Are you really fine with that?

57:39.560 --> 57:42.690
Seriously, would you shut up, Segawa?!

57:42.690 --> 57:47.450
If you're frustrated about having to scrap work,
why don't you channel that frustration into something new?

57:47.450 --> 57:52.360
Fine, just keep sulking, holding grudges, and refusing to move on.

57:52.360 --> 57:52.940
Idiot.

57:56.070 --> 57:58.170
No, don't call it a failure.

57:58.170 --> 58:01.330
I probably hurt Endou's feelings.

58:02.190 --> 58:04.210
Seeing him so low just eats away at me.

58:04.210 --> 58:07.920
That's why I agreed to talk some sense into him when Shimoyanagi asked me.

58:08.390 --> 58:11.230
But all I did was act patronizing.

58:11.230 --> 58:14.420
I'm sure Endou is regretting what he said right about now too.

58:14.820 --> 58:20.430
People've told me to stop driving people into a corner just arguing without compassion.

58:20.430 --> 58:21.870
That's not...

58:25.140 --> 58:29.060
I hear octopuses can escape through a gap as small as one centimeter.

58:29.060 --> 58:30.410
Isn't that awesome?

58:30.410 --> 58:31.820
Who cares?

58:31.820 --> 58:35.900
I don't want to animate it without having a good understanding of it first.

58:35.900 --> 58:37.280
What, it's for work?

58:37.280 --> 58:40.540
I did a giant centipede the other day.
Now that was a challenge.

58:40.540 --> 58:41.410
That's nothing special.

58:41.410 --> 58:43.880
Really? You think so?

58:41.840 --> 58:45.800
Now, it's time for our special trick!

58:43.880 --> 58:49.490
Oh yeah, the Exodus episode where the girls fall into a snake pit was great.

58:45.800 --> 58:49.280
If he succeeds, reward him with a big round of applause!

58:49.490 --> 58:50.790
Snakes all over the ground.

58:51.180 --> 58:54.530
And the Time Hippo scene where they run down a crumbling Buddha statue.

58:54.530 --> 58:56.300
The keyframes looked great.

58:56.300 --> 58:58.960
I wish I could've seen the finished product.

58:58.960 --> 59:02.310
Please. I'm sure Kitano would have done it way better.

59:02.310 --> 59:05.680
SIVA is looking good. I know it's gonna turn out great.

59:07.180 --> 59:09.120
Looks right up your alley, you know.

59:09.120 --> 59:10.820
What are you trying to get at?

59:10.820 --> 59:13.320
I'm saying I wish you'd help out with it.

59:13.320 --> 59:15.600
I wanted to work on Time Hippo!

59:15.600 --> 59:18.390
Not some movie with a nonsensical title.

59:18.390 --> 59:20.170
It's not the title you're working for.

59:20.170 --> 59:23.380
Motivation is more primal and instinctive than that.

59:23.380 --> 59:27.060
You call me all the way out here just to give me a lecture?

59:27.060 --> 59:29.040
No, I'm giving you an offer by proxy.

59:29.040 --> 59:29.830
What?

59:29.830 --> 59:34.960
The director and Miyamori really want you to design SIVA.

59:34.960 --> 59:38.230
They want you to draw a huge, showy, bulky ship.

59:38.230 --> 59:39.150
I'm not up for it.

59:39.150 --> 59:42.090
I read the story. It's super over the top and fun.

59:42.090 --> 59:45.760
You need to work on that movie.

59:45.760 --> 59:47.460
You sure are a smooth talker.

59:49.130 --> 59:52.730
If you draw SIVA, I'll animate the hell out of it.

59:52.730 --> 59:53.880
Don't you want to see that?

59:54.980 --> 59:58.130
I'm sure Segawa would say the same thing.

59:59.150 --> 01:00:02.070
Tell me what you'd do with SIVA.

01:00:05.650 --> 01:00:07.420
I'm off!

01:00:07.420 --> 01:00:08.700
See you tomorrow, Endou!

01:00:11.370 --> 01:00:12.710
Mayumi!

01:00:13.300 --> 01:00:14.590
Endou!

01:00:14.590 --> 01:00:17.250
What's up? You don't usually drop by here.

01:00:17.250 --> 01:00:18.320
What, I can't stop by?

01:00:18.320 --> 01:00:20.550
Of course you can, silly.

01:00:23.720 --> 01:00:29.950
Mitani from the meat counter told me that
you've gotta fry raw liver before doing anything else to it.

01:00:29.950 --> 01:00:31.360
I'll try that someday.

01:00:31.360 --> 01:00:33.570
You don't have to bother. I'm not a fan of it anyway.

01:00:33.570 --> 01:00:38.220
Oh, shush! It's my mission in life to cure you of your picky eating.

01:00:38.220 --> 01:00:39.850
Mission in life?

01:00:40.500 --> 01:00:43.200
Did something good happen today?

01:00:44.020 --> 01:00:46.730
It's been a while since you've actually sounded happy.

01:00:48.450 --> 01:00:49.450
Here.

01:00:49.450 --> 01:00:52.160
Just for today, to celebrate all our blessings.

01:00:52.160 --> 01:00:54.170
Though drinking here is a bit ill-mannered.

01:00:54.170 --> 01:00:56.360
Blessings? Like what?

01:00:56.360 --> 01:00:59.010
You have a lot of work, and your husband won't get a job...

01:00:59.010 --> 01:01:02.140
I'm happy just to be with you,

01:01:02.140 --> 01:01:04.840
so little things like that couldn't ever bring me down.

01:01:06.820 --> 01:01:09.230
I know how amazing you are.

01:01:10.980 --> 01:01:14.290
But I do hope someday I'll get to watch another amazing anime you made.

01:01:24.710 --> 01:01:26.430
Another blessing.

01:01:31.700 --> 01:01:32.910
Hits the spot.

01:01:37.370 --> 01:01:42.010
Starting today, Endou will be joining us as an action AD and mechanical designer!

01:01:42.010 --> 01:01:44.010
Wow! It's Endou Ryousuke!

01:01:44.010 --> 01:01:45.270
As well as...

01:01:45.270 --> 01:01:48.620
Andou Tsubaki, here on loan from Dropfit Studio!

01:01:48.620 --> 01:01:50.390
It's great to be here!

01:01:50.390 --> 01:01:52.570
No way! How come you're here?

01:01:52.570 --> 01:01:55.310
Prodigal daughter Andou, here to help!

01:01:55.310 --> 01:01:57.010
Great, counting on you, then.

01:01:57.010 --> 01:02:01.400
Watanabe, don't you have any closing words like the old president, Marukawa?

01:02:01.400 --> 01:02:04.030
I'm not him. I end the meetings normally.

01:02:04.030 --> 01:02:06.770
It's an amphibious assault ship,
so how about "full speed ahead"?

01:02:06.770 --> 01:02:08.030
I told you, I'm not—

01:02:08.030 --> 01:02:09.800
Musani, raise the sails!

01:02:09.800 --> 01:02:10.660
Full speed ahead!

01:02:10.660 --> 01:02:12.360
Full speed ahead!

01:02:12.360 --> 01:02:13.400
<i>Understood.</i>

01:02:13.400 --> 01:02:16.270
<i>Right now we have the designs for the main characters and the main ship,</i>

01:02:16.270 --> 01:02:17.710
<i>so would you mind having a look?</i>

01:02:17.710 --> 01:02:19.960
<i>When would you happen to be available?</i>

01:02:19.960 --> 01:02:23.590
<i>It depends on the storyboards, but we're aiming to have the animation done by the middle of August.</i>

01:02:23.590 --> 01:02:26.420
<i>I'll contact you again once the storyboards are done.</i>

01:02:26.420 --> 01:02:28.590
Wow, took you long enough.

01:02:28.590 --> 01:02:29.980
I was waiting for you to call.

01:02:29.980 --> 01:02:31.720
Don't be such a stranger, Andou.

01:02:31.720 --> 01:02:35.100
Huh? Yeah, I definitely won't let you down this time.

01:02:35.100 --> 01:02:39.190
What? Right now? I'm 100% busy worki—

01:02:39.870 --> 01:02:41.490
Well, I've got the window open.

01:02:42.560 --> 01:02:46.490
I humbly accept your offer to join as an animation director.

01:02:46.490 --> 01:02:50.870
I am truly grateful that you accepted despite your busy schedule.

01:02:52.740 --> 01:02:54.120
Thank goodness!

01:02:54.120 --> 01:02:56.500
Do you know the total estimate for shots and frames?

01:02:56.500 --> 01:02:57.340
Huh?

01:02:57.340 --> 01:02:59.880
Once I know that, I can estimate the amount of work.

01:02:59.880 --> 01:03:04.220
Based on the look of things,
when will the schedule be the busiest?

01:03:04.220 --> 01:03:07.880
How many keyframes should I plan to have to check in a day then?

01:03:07.880 --> 01:03:08.910
Um...

01:03:08.910 --> 01:03:12.140
You'll be working all that out, right?

01:03:12.140 --> 01:03:13.510
Um, yeah...

01:03:13.510 --> 01:03:16.650
Just don't show up with work and expect it back the same day, okay?

01:03:16.650 --> 01:03:19.370
And don't skip AD check to speed things up.

01:03:19.370 --> 01:03:21.040
At least make sure you contact me.

01:03:21.830 --> 01:03:22.610
I'll do my best!

01:03:23.010 --> 01:03:24.980
Is this okay for Hedwig?

01:03:24.980 --> 01:03:25.970
Hey, I like—

01:03:24.980 --> 01:03:26.860
It looks absolutely marvelous!

01:03:26.860 --> 01:03:29.490
Seems I've got the assistant's seal of approval.

01:03:29.830 --> 01:03:31.000
And you, Director?

01:03:31.000 --> 01:03:34.520
Yeah, it's good! I wanted to be the first to say it.

01:03:34.520 --> 01:03:36.500
Time for the side characters, then.

01:03:36.500 --> 01:03:38.500
Endou's done with the assault ship too!

01:03:39.770 --> 01:03:44.630
For the lines, I was thinking of having us process them during filming to make it look hand drawn.

01:03:44.630 --> 01:03:45.560
Not bad.

01:03:45.560 --> 01:03:50.540
It'll have to be toned down for TV, but we can go all out with the color for the cinemas.

01:03:50.540 --> 01:03:52.890
Nebulas... Dust clouds...

01:03:53.310 --> 01:03:56.890
Clouds indicating a stellar world out of humanity's grasp...

01:03:57.250 --> 01:03:59.740
Solitude... Hope...

01:03:59.740 --> 01:04:01.220
Doesn't it look a bit dark?

01:04:01.220 --> 01:04:03.280
Maybe I should make the character brighter.

01:04:03.280 --> 01:04:07.780
But if it's any brighter than this, won't it look out of place on Atsumi's backgrounds?

01:04:07.780 --> 01:04:10.180
Also, regarding the bow wave effect for the ship...

01:04:10.180 --> 01:04:13.510
Yeah, about that... Do we really need a bow wave in space?

01:04:13.510 --> 01:04:15.780
Apparently the director's insisting.

01:04:15.780 --> 01:04:16.540
All right, got it.

01:04:16.540 --> 01:04:21.420
Yeah, well, normally we'd want the storyboard done before we get started on the music...

01:04:21.420 --> 01:04:24.860
I mean, film scoring would be ideal, but...

01:04:24.860 --> 01:04:25.920
Sorry.

01:04:25.920 --> 01:04:29.420
So for M-15, "The enemies' boring everyday life,"

01:04:29.420 --> 01:04:33.300
how exactly are you going to portray the enemies' everyday life?

01:04:33.300 --> 01:04:38.730
Well, they're nervous, but they also somehow have their guard down and seem distant...

01:04:38.730 --> 01:04:39.680
To be more specific...

01:04:43.960 --> 01:04:46.320
Basically, cheap synth music.

01:04:46.320 --> 01:04:48.040
Yeah, exactly, synth music.

01:04:48.040 --> 01:04:50.500
So... Something like this?

01:04:52.750 --> 01:04:54.930
Could you do it a bit more like... tap-tatap?

01:04:54.930 --> 01:04:56.130
Tap-tatap?

01:04:57.730 --> 01:05:00.830
So basically, um... What's the right word...

01:05:01.320 --> 01:05:03.210
Like Western, uh, <i>you know</i>?

01:05:03.210 --> 01:05:05.460
Yeah, that's right, <i>Western stuff</i>.

01:05:05.460 --> 01:05:06.750
Do you follow?

01:05:06.750 --> 01:05:09.090
Well... How about this?

01:05:12.970 --> 01:05:14.210
Yes, that's exactly it!

01:05:14.210 --> 01:05:15.170
Sounds good.

01:05:15.170 --> 01:05:16.280
Western what?

01:05:16.280 --> 01:05:17.850
Girls don't need to understand.

01:05:17.850 --> 01:05:20.350
Huh... A movie at Musani...

01:05:20.350 --> 01:05:22.860
Something-something-ship SIVA, it's called.

01:05:22.860 --> 01:05:27.230
SIVA? Wasn't GePeU working on something with the same name?

01:05:27.520 --> 01:05:32.990
Voice actors, entertainers and talents still belong to slightly different categories, right?

01:05:33.300 --> 01:05:38.230
I'm hoping that you'll become someone who transcends those categories one day.

01:05:38.230 --> 01:05:38.910
I'm sorry, but...

01:05:39.570 --> 01:05:42.040
There's an anime I'd like to audition for.

01:05:42.290 --> 01:05:44.420
I've gotta admire your enthusiasm...

01:05:44.420 --> 01:05:46.560
I do think you're taking good care of me here.

01:05:46.560 --> 01:05:51.040
But if I don't try now, I think I'll regret it one day.

01:05:51.040 --> 01:05:53.740
Right now you're well-known for your on-camera work.

01:05:53.740 --> 01:05:56.090
But we don't know how you'll perform as a VA.

01:05:56.090 --> 01:05:58.300
There's no guarantee that you'll be as well-received.

01:05:58.300 --> 01:05:59.730
I'm aware of that.

01:05:59.730 --> 01:06:01.560
But I'd still like to give it a go.

01:06:02.190 --> 01:06:04.060
"Natto. The forbidden food."

01:06:04.060 --> 01:06:06.810
Can I think of this as just normal natto?

01:06:06.810 --> 01:06:10.110
That's correct. The product itself is just normal natto with small beans.

01:06:10.110 --> 01:06:13.780
But try to make it look like they're really shoveling it down.

01:06:13.780 --> 01:06:15.060
Very well.

01:06:15.060 --> 01:06:18.310
I can't even imagine what a natto scene by you would look like.

01:06:18.310 --> 01:06:19.660
Can't wait!

01:06:19.660 --> 01:06:22.830
I'll be counting on you for any corrections,

01:06:22.830 --> 01:06:23.840
Yasuhara.

01:06:23.840 --> 01:06:27.210
Huh? Oh, uh... I look forward to working with you too.

01:06:27.210 --> 01:06:29.210
A Musani anime movie?!

01:06:29.210 --> 01:06:32.720
I'd like you to be the chief animator. What do you think?

01:06:32.720 --> 01:06:33.340
I'll do it!

01:06:34.780 --> 01:06:36.220
Now, as for Rally...

01:06:36.220 --> 01:06:37.390
I'll finish up on Rally, too!

01:06:37.390 --> 01:06:39.010
That's impossible, schedule-wise.

01:06:39.010 --> 01:06:41.980
But I don't want to abandon it partway!

01:06:41.980 --> 01:06:43.100
Oh, fine.

01:06:44.370 --> 01:06:48.200
I swore never to repeat the same mistake.

01:06:48.200 --> 01:06:49.560
I understand.

01:06:49.560 --> 01:06:51.660
The second meeting room is available now!

01:06:51.660 --> 01:06:54.310
Could we use it from 4 pm?

01:06:54.310 --> 01:06:55.440
Let me check!

01:06:55.440 --> 01:06:57.070
You sure seem busy.

01:06:57.360 --> 01:06:58.820
Mr. Sugie!

01:06:58.820 --> 01:06:59.950
You're the same as always.

01:06:59.950 --> 01:07:01.160
Not at all.

01:07:01.160 --> 01:07:01.780
Your beard!

01:07:02.140 --> 01:07:04.250
Oh, yeah... Does it look strange?

01:07:04.250 --> 01:07:04.790
Not at all.

01:07:05.210 --> 01:07:09.920
My wife's been scolding me about getting too sloppy since I started working from home.

01:07:09.920 --> 01:07:12.460
I think it looks really good on you!

01:07:12.460 --> 01:07:14.310
Oh, are you here for Watanabe?

01:07:14.310 --> 01:07:16.550
No, no, I'm just here to ask a favor.

01:07:16.850 --> 01:07:20.840
I'll be holding an anime class at the civic center in October.

01:07:20.840 --> 01:07:23.950
I've got to stave off senility somehow.

01:07:23.950 --> 01:07:25.970
You'll be the one teaching?

01:07:25.970 --> 01:07:27.060
Yes, I was asked to.

01:07:27.430 --> 01:07:31.800
I'll draw pictures with the children and then have fun by making the drawings move.

01:07:31.800 --> 01:07:35.070
Right now, I'm looking for someone to help out.

01:07:35.070 --> 01:07:37.570
Understood! I'll try asking around.

01:07:37.900 --> 01:07:40.410
Also, I have a request of my own!

01:07:40.410 --> 01:07:41.410
Huh?

01:07:41.410 --> 01:07:44.330
I'd love for you to draw the scene where these pegacorns fly!

01:07:44.770 --> 01:07:46.660
Do I just animate them like horses?

01:07:46.660 --> 01:07:47.610
That would be fine.

01:07:47.610 --> 01:07:52.130
You animated the march of the dancing man-eating bears in Two Piece, right?

01:07:52.130 --> 01:07:53.670
Something like that would be great.

01:07:53.670 --> 01:07:56.840
So they're not flying, but running through the air.

01:07:56.840 --> 01:07:58.940
Here are the designs and some reference video.

01:07:58.940 --> 01:08:01.260
I'm basically a retiree at this point, you know.

01:08:01.260 --> 01:08:03.010
Now, now.

01:08:03.670 --> 01:08:05.720
You've grown tougher, Miyamori.

01:08:06.270 --> 01:08:07.560
Oh, sorry about that.

01:08:07.560 --> 01:08:09.730
And you're more cheerful too.

01:08:09.730 --> 01:08:13.480
Can I count on you for the other end of the bargain, then?

01:08:13.480 --> 01:08:19.870
Director, do you want to get more information on the enemy captain's model car collecting hobby?

01:08:19.870 --> 01:08:24.000
Well, there's a script meeting today anyway. We'll probably learn more there.

01:08:24.000 --> 01:08:27.740
I'm sorry, Director, but we're skipping today's script meeting.

01:08:27.740 --> 01:08:31.420
There was no meeting last week either, right? What did Maitake say?

01:08:31.420 --> 01:08:33.380
He's having trouble deciding on the story.

01:08:35.410 --> 01:08:39.010
Could we have the meeting anyway? It's fine if it drags on.

01:08:39.010 --> 01:08:41.120
I'll run it by the others.

01:08:41.120 --> 01:08:44.540
Maybe we can think of something if we rack our brains together.

01:08:44.540 --> 01:08:46.560
Do you mind if I sit in too?

01:08:46.560 --> 01:08:47.390
Sure thing.

01:08:47.720 --> 01:08:52.640
I originally wrote that they evade all the enemy's attacks and make a brilliant escape,

01:08:52.640 --> 01:08:55.660
and most would probably say that that's the correct choice.

01:08:55.660 --> 01:08:59.650
The viewers would accept it, and it's enjoyable. I don't see the problem.

01:08:59.650 --> 01:09:04.070
Sorry for being vague here,
but it just seems like a fantasy.

01:09:04.070 --> 01:09:07.520
Well, I mean, it's fiction, so it's a fantasy either way...

01:09:07.520 --> 01:09:11.880
But I just can't come to terms with this plot line.

01:09:11.880 --> 01:09:16.600
Also, I'm starting to wonder what the point of having Arte even is.

01:09:16.600 --> 01:09:21.310
But you had a bunch of ideas for her, like her secretly having a history with Hedwig?

01:09:21.310 --> 01:09:23.820
And that part just feels excessive.

01:09:23.820 --> 01:09:28.430
It's a good idea in and of itself, but it's difficult to incorporate it in the drama, or like...

01:09:28.720 --> 01:09:31.130
Shame, Iguchi's character design for her is great.

01:09:31.130 --> 01:09:33.810
I wanted to see more of her, if anything.

01:09:33.810 --> 01:09:35.880
Yes, I do understand you...

01:09:35.880 --> 01:09:39.840
Well, in the end, just go with whatever works for you!

01:09:39.840 --> 01:09:41.310
That's right, whatever's easiest!

01:09:41.310 --> 01:09:43.450
Exactly, whatever you want!

01:09:44.120 --> 01:09:47.500
Sorry, I'm happy that you all gathered here just for me,

01:09:47.500 --> 01:09:49.670
but you just made me more confused.

01:09:51.890 --> 01:09:55.710
I hope I didn't upset Maitake... Think he's angry?

01:09:55.710 --> 01:09:59.070
Nah, surely not. It's Maitake we're talking about.

01:09:57.040 --> 01:10:00.710
6 Months Until Premiere

01:09:59.070 --> 01:09:59.910
Right?

01:10:00.710 --> 01:10:03.330
In this segment, we'll be discussing upcoming events.

01:10:00.720 --> 01:10:04.260
EntR

01:10:00.720 --> 01:10:04.260
Hot New Anime

01:10:00.720 --> 01:10:04.260
What will become of Tadatsugu?

01:10:03.330 --> 01:10:07.890
Next month is the long-awaited premiere of Bride and Raven, from the esteemed director Yamada Masashi.

01:10:07.890 --> 01:10:29.080
Hot New Anime

01:10:07.890 --> 01:10:22.320
What will become of Tadatsugu?

01:10:10.390 --> 01:10:14.860
You for real? Try again when you've learned to fly, stupid.

01:10:14.860 --> 01:10:17.810
Just you wait! Don't forget those words when I'm up there flying!

01:10:19.310 --> 01:10:22.320
Like I ever would, stupid! Stupid!

01:10:22.320 --> 01:10:26.240
Today, we have Director Yamada with us as a special guest.

01:10:26.240 --> 01:10:30.700
Hello, everyone's beloved Yamada Masashi, at'cha service!

01:10:32.960 --> 01:10:35.120
Hey, it's looking pretty good.

01:10:35.120 --> 01:10:38.710
Can you make the lines look a bit more... refined, or hand-drawn?

01:10:38.710 --> 01:10:40.680
Should I make the outlines thicker?

01:10:40.680 --> 01:10:45.590
No, it's just that Endou's design and your model feel a bit different, Toudou.

01:10:45.590 --> 01:10:49.900
Could you bring out more of Endou's style, or allure so to speak?

01:10:49.900 --> 01:10:52.970
Come on, that's just an idiosyncrasy of mine.

01:10:51.970 --> 01:10:52.970
I'll give it a go!

01:10:53.670 --> 01:10:54.880
I want to try.

01:10:54.880 --> 01:11:00.860
I want to try and bring the oft-denounced
CG-ishness closer to the hand-drawn style!

01:11:00.860 --> 01:11:03.110
Please have some. They're from Honda.

01:11:03.110 --> 01:11:04.480
Don't mind if I do!

01:11:04.480 --> 01:11:07.740
Since I quit smoking, I've really developed a sweet tooth.

01:11:07.740 --> 01:11:09.710
You're headed down Honda's path, you know.

01:11:09.710 --> 01:11:12.870
Oh, yeah... Honda's, and our departed virtuoso's.

01:11:12.870 --> 01:11:14.130
Virtuoso?

01:11:14.130 --> 01:11:16.370
B&R's director Yamada Masashi.

01:11:16.370 --> 01:11:16.980
Oh.

01:11:16.980 --> 01:11:17.790
Breaking!

01:11:17.790 --> 01:11:20.380
The virtuoso Director Yamada accused of using casting couch!

01:11:20.380 --> 01:11:21.880
What?!

01:11:22.260 --> 01:11:23.870
This has to be fake.

01:11:23.870 --> 01:11:26.370
As if Yamada would do something like this.

01:11:26.370 --> 01:11:28.450
They say people change, though.

01:11:28.450 --> 01:11:30.390
He probably let it go to his head.

01:11:30.390 --> 01:11:31.840
I know what it's like.

01:11:31.840 --> 01:11:35.750
The director called off today's livestream on short notice, citing illness.

01:11:35.750 --> 01:11:37.520
Canceled... In that case...

01:11:37.890 --> 01:11:40.520
Maybe he'd help out with SIVA?

01:11:40.520 --> 01:11:41.690
That's your first thought?!

01:11:40.520 --> 01:11:41.690
What?!

01:11:42.370 --> 01:11:43.770
He won't pick up.

01:11:44.150 --> 01:11:47.180
We've already handed them the auditioning scripts.

01:11:47.180 --> 01:11:49.400
Would you like to explain the movie first, Direct—

01:11:49.400 --> 01:11:50.690
That's a bad idea!

01:11:50.690 --> 01:11:53.410
I wouldn't want to get so close to the VAs that it turns into a scandal!

01:11:54.580 --> 01:11:56.520
Can't you at least answer whatever questions they—

01:11:56.520 --> 01:11:57.850
No can do! Danger ahead!

01:11:57.850 --> 01:12:00.710
No women other than Mom,
my ex, and Seira are allowed close!

01:12:00.710 --> 01:12:02.540
What a pain...

01:12:09.380 --> 01:12:10.550
Maitake!

01:12:10.810 --> 01:12:12.350
Good morning!

01:12:12.930 --> 01:12:16.180
Maitake! C'mon, have a seat. Yep, right here.

01:12:14.520 --> 01:12:16.180
Oh, thanks...

01:12:19.930 --> 01:12:22.690
You weakling! There's no such thing as a miracle!

01:12:22.690 --> 01:12:25.070
You have to seize your own destiny!

01:12:25.070 --> 01:12:26.440
You weakling!

01:12:26.440 --> 01:12:27.690
There's no such thing as a miracle!

01:12:27.690 --> 01:12:29.650
You have to seize your own destiny.

01:12:29.650 --> 01:12:31.030
You weakling!

01:12:31.030 --> 01:12:32.320
There's no such thing as a miracle.

01:12:32.320 --> 01:12:34.530
You have to seize your own destiny!

01:12:35.240 --> 01:12:36.790
I see...

01:12:36.790 --> 01:12:39.910
I was imagining someone a bit more brusque.

01:12:39.910 --> 01:12:44.830
Madoka said he thought of Arte as kind of boorish.

01:12:44.830 --> 01:12:47.920
Well, she does start out as a cafeteria lady,

01:12:47.920 --> 01:12:54.010
but fundamentally she's someone with
both a foolhardy and a delicate side.

01:12:54.010 --> 01:12:55.470
That's how I view her.

01:12:56.920 --> 01:13:01.770
Say you've got realism here,
and more cartoonish styles here.

01:13:01.770 --> 01:13:02.670
Right...

01:13:02.670 --> 01:13:06.690
If I'm looking critically at something like Yamada's realistic character acting,

01:13:06.690 --> 01:13:10.070
I prefer exaggerated, easy-to-understand acting, and I'm better at it too.

01:13:10.480 --> 01:13:13.450
There's no point if it doesn't come across.

01:13:14.640 --> 01:13:18.660
It's pretty, all right, but it's the beauty of stills.

01:13:19.290 --> 01:13:21.500
Nothing but natto day in, day out!

01:13:21.500 --> 01:13:23.320
Natto, natto, natto, natto!

01:13:23.320 --> 01:13:25.710
I've had enough! I can't take it anymore!

01:13:26.260 --> 01:13:28.050
Great, thank you.

01:13:28.570 --> 01:13:29.710
Thank you.

01:13:30.330 --> 01:13:31.560
It's Lucy.

01:13:31.560 --> 01:13:33.220
Well, yes, it's Lucy.

01:13:33.220 --> 01:13:35.220
Could you have her do Arte too?

01:13:35.620 --> 01:13:37.920
Huh? That's a completely different character!

01:13:37.920 --> 01:13:39.730
Well, I just want to see what she'd be like.

01:13:39.730 --> 01:13:42.440
Sakaki, do you have Arte's script on you?

01:13:42.440 --> 01:13:43.480
Huh? Arte's?

01:13:43.480 --> 01:13:45.990
Yeah, of course not. Could you go hand it to her?

01:13:45.990 --> 01:13:47.110
At once!

01:13:47.820 --> 01:13:51.860
There's no such thing as a miracle.
You have to seize your own destiny!

01:13:51.860 --> 01:13:53.850
I could never accept it.

01:13:53.850 --> 01:13:56.280
Why can't we go where we want freely?

01:13:56.280 --> 01:13:58.500
Why is there a limit to what we can do?

01:13:58.500 --> 01:14:00.260
Great, thank you.

01:14:00.260 --> 01:14:01.500
Thank you.

01:14:03.810 --> 01:14:05.000
Can I go home?

01:14:05.760 --> 01:14:07.410
Huh? Why? Did I do something?

01:14:07.410 --> 01:14:09.010
No, I want to get to work.

01:14:09.010 --> 01:14:11.010
We'll contact you again at a later date.

01:14:11.010 --> 01:14:13.670
Would it be possible to get a screenwriter assistant on board?

01:14:13.670 --> 01:14:15.390
I know I'm the one who caused the delay, but...

01:14:15.390 --> 01:14:17.470
Don't tell me you're shoving the climax on someone else?!

01:14:17.470 --> 01:14:18.890
No, no, the opposite.

01:14:19.170 --> 01:14:22.390
I'll write it all to the end, but I need some ideas.

01:14:26.070 --> 01:14:28.260
What parts do you think are lacking?

01:14:28.260 --> 01:14:30.120
Can I be blunt?

01:14:30.120 --> 01:14:32.310
Please provide me your unreserved opinion.

01:14:32.310 --> 01:14:35.310
The girls just seem like plot devices to me.

01:14:35.930 --> 01:14:39.670
I think Arte started to change after the dining scene,

01:14:39.670 --> 01:14:42.540
but since it's intentionally shown later, it's difficult to see.

01:14:42.540 --> 01:14:45.410
But there's no fun in just showing it like normal, right?

01:14:45.410 --> 01:14:48.910
Yeah, it might hurt the character development and the drama.

01:14:50.350 --> 01:14:53.310
It's more or less okay, but when it really comes down to it...

01:14:53.310 --> 01:14:55.750
Well, that's why I'm asking you,

01:14:55.750 --> 01:14:56.930
miss screenwriter.

01:14:56.930 --> 01:14:59.170
No, I'm talking about my pitching.

01:14:59.170 --> 01:15:02.100
I wrote the script for Quick Motion Story.

01:15:02.100 --> 01:15:05.280
I'm more or less able to throw curveballs and forkballs now.

01:15:07.220 --> 01:15:09.850
Oh, I'm sorry! It's still a bit difficult.

01:15:09.850 --> 01:15:12.440
Like they say, pitchers aren't athletes, huh?

01:15:12.830 --> 01:15:16.560
Master, what do you think is most important when it comes to pitching?

01:15:16.560 --> 01:15:19.200
Speed? Pitch type? Control?

01:15:19.200 --> 01:15:22.660
Doesn't matter what kind of ball you throw if it doesn't make it to the plate.

01:15:23.000 --> 01:15:25.410
Now, let's continue the discussion.

01:15:25.410 --> 01:15:29.290
What's wrong with my pitches? How would you throw it, Imai?

01:15:29.920 --> 01:15:31.370
Good question...

01:15:32.040 --> 01:15:33.540
If it were me...

01:15:40.180 --> 01:15:45.180
Personally, now that I'm seeing Ogasawara's rough keyframes side-by-side with your corrections,

01:15:45.180 --> 01:15:49.380
I think while it did come out cleaner, the sense of motion has suffered.

01:15:49.380 --> 01:15:51.960
I did my best to match the model sheet...

01:15:51.960 --> 01:15:54.570
Yes, that's certainly important.

01:15:54.570 --> 01:15:57.160
But that's not enough, is it?

01:15:57.160 --> 01:15:59.070
I'm... not enough?

01:16:05.330 --> 01:16:10.080
My corrections aren't good enough, and I'm slow too. I can't just focus on one of those either.

01:16:10.680 --> 01:16:13.260
If I can't strike a balance, it's worthless.

01:16:16.420 --> 01:16:19.050
Good morning. I'm here to pick up my script.

01:16:19.050 --> 01:16:20.870
Good morning.

01:16:20.870 --> 01:16:21.800
Here you go.

01:16:23.190 --> 01:16:24.300
Um...

01:16:24.300 --> 01:16:27.720
Did you get the results from my SIVA audition yet?

01:16:27.720 --> 01:16:29.890
No, I haven't heard anything.

01:16:29.890 --> 01:16:31.560
I see...

01:16:32.760 --> 01:16:34.750
I'll let you know as soon as I get word.

01:16:34.750 --> 01:16:37.320
I know how much you wanted to do it.

01:16:37.320 --> 01:16:40.700
So if you don't say what you want to do, it's over before it started.

01:16:41.470 --> 01:16:47.330
But someone like me requesting work seems kind of presumptuous or arrogant.

01:16:47.330 --> 01:16:51.000
And if we really flunk the audition,
we'll be causing trouble for the agency.

01:16:51.000 --> 01:16:55.340
But I don't think that should keep you from saying what you think and what you want.

01:16:55.340 --> 01:16:57.300
Is it really okay for us to do that?

01:16:57.300 --> 01:16:59.710
You just need confidence and determination.

01:17:02.440 --> 01:17:05.900
And with that, it's finalized. Thank you all very much.

01:17:05.900 --> 01:17:07.850
Thank you.

01:17:07.010 --> 01:17:08.350
We're finally done.

01:17:08.350 --> 01:17:11.850
I'm really sorry about dragging it out like this.

01:17:11.850 --> 01:17:14.110
So it ends in defeat, not victory.

01:17:14.110 --> 01:17:16.980
But there's still something satisfactory about it.

01:17:16.980 --> 01:17:18.600
I think it's a fitting outcome.

01:17:18.600 --> 01:17:21.770
And I'm so happy Hedwig's feelings got requited in the end.

01:17:21.770 --> 01:17:23.740
That was Imai's idea.

01:17:24.370 --> 01:17:25.870
Oh, no, that's...

01:17:25.870 --> 01:17:30.230
Thank you, Imai. If not for you, I'd still be struggling.

01:17:30.230 --> 01:17:31.750
Please don't, master!

01:17:31.750 --> 01:17:35.000
I'm not your master. I'm your business rival.

01:17:43.650 --> 01:17:45.430
Do you have business with us?

01:17:46.400 --> 01:17:47.890
Yamada.

01:17:47.890 --> 01:17:49.760
Here to repent, huh?

01:17:49.760 --> 01:17:51.320
No! I didn't do it!

01:17:51.320 --> 01:17:52.890
Please, hear me out!

01:17:52.890 --> 01:17:55.090
Well, I don't really care either way.

01:17:55.090 --> 01:17:57.760
If people are fawning over you,
you're still a greenhorn.

01:17:57.760 --> 01:17:59.480
When you get flamed is when it starts for real.

01:17:59.480 --> 01:18:00.800
When what starts?

01:18:00.800 --> 01:18:02.330
Your work as a director.

01:18:02.330 --> 01:18:04.700
And it's still just the second time.
Don't worry about it.

01:18:04.700 --> 01:18:06.520
Second? When was the first?

01:18:06.520 --> 01:18:08.780
You know, when Beyond Jiggly blew up.

01:18:08.780 --> 01:18:10.460
That was your fault!

01:18:10.460 --> 01:18:11.540
Huh? Was it?

01:18:11.540 --> 01:18:14.200
I understand everyone's sentiments and anger,

01:18:14.200 --> 01:18:16.480
but this thing is just a mean-spirited photoshop!

01:18:16.480 --> 01:18:17.670
What? Really?

01:18:17.670 --> 01:18:19.170
Yes, it is!

01:18:20.720 --> 01:18:23.510
This is just a question of brightness.

01:18:23.510 --> 01:18:26.120
And sharpen it a bit...

01:18:29.010 --> 01:18:30.940
It's MakuradaP and EnjouP!

01:18:30.940 --> 01:18:33.400
That's right, they were right behind me...

01:18:33.400 --> 01:18:35.190
Pfft, just a closing party photo?

01:18:35.190 --> 01:18:37.020
Don't talk like you're disappointed.

01:18:37.020 --> 01:18:39.290
One's fifteen minutes of fame expire quickly.

01:18:39.290 --> 01:18:42.640
I'll just have to trust in that and wait for the storm to pass.

01:18:42.640 --> 01:18:45.520
That storm's gonna follow you around the rest of your life.

01:18:45.520 --> 01:18:47.730
It would be best to make a public apology.

01:18:47.730 --> 01:18:48.950
Do you think they'll believe me?

01:18:48.950 --> 01:18:50.910
I'm sure a lot won't.

01:18:50.910 --> 01:18:54.870
Even so, it's not like it could turn out worse than now.

01:18:54.870 --> 01:18:56.920
And you <i>did</i> get carried away.

01:19:01.720 --> 01:19:01.760
• Apology

01:19:01.720 --> 01:19:01.760
• Let me teach you about the creatures known as kittens

01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:01.800
What happened was a result of my own carelessness

01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:01.800
and naivete, and I truly regret my actions. I had grown

01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:01.800
conceited, forgetting that I'm only a creator thanks of

01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:01.800
all my fans, my staff, and everyone else who supports

01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:01.800
me. I apologize from the bottom of my heart. While

01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:01.800
I realize that I am in no position to make excuses for

01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:01.800
myself, I would like to take this opportunity to explain

01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:01.800
how this all came about.

01:19:03.940 --> 01:19:05.300
Oh my, the server is down.

01:19:05.300 --> 01:19:06.030
What?!

01:19:05.300 --> 01:19:12.310
This site can't be reached

01:19:05.300 --> 01:19:12.310
It took too long to respond.

01:19:06.030 --> 01:19:10.480
Oh, uh... Yamada's website is terribly slow right now.

01:19:10.480 --> 01:19:11.460
Oh, is that all?

01:19:11.460 --> 01:19:12.310
Huh?

01:19:12.310 --> 01:19:14.440
I hope this is enough to calm things down.

01:19:14.440 --> 01:19:15.210
Right?

01:19:15.210 --> 01:19:17.220
If it spreads to us, SIVA will suffer.

01:19:17.220 --> 01:19:20.630
We'll just take it as it comes.
We've done all we can for now.

01:19:20.630 --> 01:19:25.110
No matter how sincere you are, sometimes you just can't get through to people.

01:19:26.320 --> 01:19:28.570
Now I just need two more people for both production and directing.

01:19:29.500 --> 01:19:31.880
The hero always arrives late.

01:19:32.490 --> 01:19:33.580
Ta-dah!

01:19:33.580 --> 01:19:35.200
Just go in already.

01:19:35.200 --> 01:19:36.860
Hey, not too shabby.

01:19:36.860 --> 01:19:41.130
And hey, didn't you steal this from me? A sci-fi space drama...

01:19:41.130 --> 01:19:43.870
Whatever you say. Now, what are your schedules looking like?

01:19:43.870 --> 01:19:44.950
We can start right away.

01:19:44.950 --> 01:19:47.140
Hey, why do you get to decide my schedule?

01:19:47.140 --> 01:19:48.970
I'm in charge of you, you know.

01:19:58.210 --> 01:20:00.850
Director, how are things coming along?

01:20:01.960 --> 01:20:03.040
Director?!

01:20:17.830 --> 01:20:18.500
Storyboards!

01:20:18.500 --> 01:20:19.580
I'm free.

01:20:19.580 --> 01:20:21.210
I'll call someone on you!

01:20:21.210 --> 01:20:23.210
Just you try!

01:20:30.630 --> 01:20:32.610
Huh? Yano? What are you doing here?

01:20:32.610 --> 01:20:35.260
Things have finally calmed down at home.

01:20:36.170 --> 01:20:38.800
Is that right? That's great to hear!

01:20:38.800 --> 01:20:40.430
I'm sorry for worrying you.

01:20:40.430 --> 01:20:43.020
Man, that's great news. Anyway, see you.

01:20:43.990 --> 01:20:46.380
And where do you think you're going?

01:20:46.380 --> 01:20:48.990
To a world without storyboards or anime.

01:20:48.990 --> 01:20:52.420
If they took anime away from you,
you'd just be left as tofu fried chicken.

01:20:52.420 --> 01:20:53.780
I wouldn't even be human?!

01:20:53.780 --> 01:20:54.890
House!

01:20:54.890 --> 01:20:55.630
Woof!

01:20:56.990 --> 01:20:58.640
Is this for real?

01:20:58.640 --> 01:20:59.490
It's for real.

01:20:59.490 --> 01:21:00.620
That's rough.

01:21:01.990 --> 01:21:03.120
Well, for starters...

01:21:07.150 --> 01:21:07.710
Director.

01:21:07.710 --> 01:21:09.250
I'm working, I'm working.

01:21:09.250 --> 01:21:10.180
Look at this.

01:21:12.380 --> 01:21:14.130
Is that... Seira?!

01:21:14.130 --> 01:21:16.720
No, it's not Kinoshita Seira.

01:21:17.050 --> 01:21:22.000
But what do you think Seira would think if she saw you right now?

01:21:23.040 --> 01:21:25.610
I'm so sorry, Seira...

01:21:25.610 --> 01:21:28.150
A fried chicken lunch!

01:21:28.990 --> 01:21:30.860
A Mont Blanc!

01:21:32.750 --> 01:21:36.520
For the sake of Seira, the fried chicken lunch, and the Mont Blanc,

01:21:36.520 --> 01:21:38.460
why don't you finish up the storyboards?

01:21:38.460 --> 01:21:41.200
But I can't think of anything.

01:21:41.200 --> 01:21:43.960
It's a complete deadlock!

01:21:43.960 --> 01:21:46.630
Wait, is it deadlock? Deadlack?

01:21:46.630 --> 01:21:48.350
Don't worry.

01:21:48.350 --> 01:21:52.340
When you've been driven into a corner is when the work starts for real.

01:21:52.340 --> 01:21:56.810
I know that you have it in you, Director.

01:21:56.810 --> 01:21:59.220
I... have it in me?

01:21:59.570 --> 01:22:00.640
That's right!

01:22:01.400 --> 01:22:02.640
Way to go.

01:22:02.640 --> 01:22:07.440
Right before the climax, their plan to escape to their home world using SIVA is discovered,

01:22:07.440 --> 01:22:10.160
Raul and Arte are captured by Captain Kouyou,

01:22:10.160 --> 01:22:13.400
and it looks as though they have to give up on everything.

01:22:13.400 --> 01:22:15.260
You weakling!

01:22:15.260 --> 01:22:18.030
There's no such thing as a miracle!
You have to seize your own destiny!

01:22:20.120 --> 01:22:21.260
Seize my own...

01:22:22.170 --> 01:22:25.870
I see! There's no point in waiting for a miracle to happen!

01:22:25.870 --> 01:22:27.960
You have to <i>make</i> them happen yourself!

01:22:28.560 --> 01:22:33.380
I'll succeed using my wits, courage, hard work, blood, sweat and tears!

01:22:35.380 --> 01:22:37.020
I will escape!

01:22:37.020 --> 01:22:43.470
I refuse to give up without seeing the outside!

01:22:46.530 --> 01:22:48.150
You did amazing.

01:22:51.730 --> 01:22:54.610
I've done all I could. I have no regrets.

01:22:54.610 --> 01:22:55.570
Are you serious?

01:22:55.570 --> 01:22:56.360
It's just starting.

01:22:56.360 --> 01:22:59.120
Don't think for a second that you're done once the storyboards are in.

01:22:59.120 --> 01:23:00.870
No way!

01:23:00.870 --> 01:23:02.220
Do we have enough unit directors?

01:23:02.220 --> 01:23:04.270
To be honest, one more would be good.

01:23:09.080 --> 01:23:13.110
Isn't there anyone who'd pay me to fish?

01:23:13.110 --> 01:23:16.130
There <i>are</i> people who'd pay you for watching films.

01:23:16.530 --> 01:23:19.510
Though by watching films, I mean quality assurance and such.

01:23:19.510 --> 01:23:21.560
Yeah, that's what I thought.

01:23:21.560 --> 01:23:22.770
It's good to see you again.

01:23:22.770 --> 01:23:23.520
How's the family?

01:23:23.520 --> 01:23:26.530
Things are sorted out enough for me to help at Musani, at least.

01:23:26.530 --> 01:23:28.510
That's good to hear.

01:23:28.510 --> 01:23:30.230
Okay, let's go, shall we?

01:23:30.230 --> 01:23:31.100
Huh?

01:23:33.650 --> 01:23:36.030
I'd say about 2 hours and 28 minutes.

01:23:36.030 --> 01:23:36.930
Too long?

01:23:36.930 --> 01:23:38.030
Too long.

01:23:38.030 --> 01:23:40.700
We're good up to 120 minutes, right?

01:23:40.700 --> 01:23:42.800
You'd have to run that by Watanabe.

01:23:42.800 --> 01:23:45.450
Maybe we should cut that natto trivia soliloquy.

01:23:45.450 --> 01:23:45.910
Sounds good.

01:23:45.910 --> 01:23:47.780
Hey, that's the part I'm in charge of!

01:23:47.780 --> 01:23:50.920
Listen here. Love for natto is powerful!

01:23:50.920 --> 01:23:56.170
It's a symbol for love, life and rebirth in this world of media of ours, got it?

01:23:56.170 --> 01:23:58.750
A symbol, huh? Those are pretty important to have.

01:23:58.750 --> 01:23:59.800
Right?!

01:23:59.800 --> 01:24:01.010
But we don't need one here.

01:24:01.010 --> 01:24:01.840
Yeah, don't need one.

01:24:01.840 --> 01:24:02.490
Don't need one.

01:24:02.490 --> 01:24:03.930
Got it.

01:24:05.980 --> 01:24:07.680
Funny story, nice shot!

01:24:07.680 --> 01:24:10.260
Dove Tengu did pretty well, huh.

01:24:10.260 --> 01:24:12.620
Yeah, really. 2.2 billion, right?

01:24:12.620 --> 01:24:14.720
Can't believe you did better than In the Center.

01:24:14.720 --> 01:24:16.440
Wish I could borrow some of your luck.

01:24:16.440 --> 01:24:19.500
But aren't you making a film of your own right now?

01:24:19.500 --> 01:24:22.340
Weren't you doing that something-or-other ship SIVA film?

01:24:22.340 --> 01:24:24.020
No, that one was shelv—

01:24:24.020 --> 01:24:24.450
This?

01:24:27.200 --> 01:24:29.210
Studio
Canabun

01:24:27.910 --> 01:24:30.510
Shimoyanagi, I'm sorry.

01:24:30.510 --> 01:24:32.360
We can't take on any more work.

01:24:32.360 --> 01:24:35.210
I can do it! I can go without sleep!

01:24:35.460 --> 01:24:37.340
That's not what this is about.

01:24:37.730 --> 01:24:40.340
I'm sorry for asking the impossible.

01:24:40.340 --> 01:24:42.340
Is that for SIVA?

01:24:42.340 --> 01:24:44.210
Yeah, but we're not—

01:24:44.210 --> 01:24:46.350
So it's an explosion and collapse scene?

01:24:46.350 --> 01:24:48.730
I'm pretty sure Okudo could pull it off.

01:24:48.730 --> 01:24:50.390
Why do you...

01:24:50.390 --> 01:24:53.730
I mean, she likes visual effects, and she's good at them too.

01:24:54.230 --> 01:24:56.940
If it's just explosions and crumbling, then probably.

01:24:56.940 --> 01:24:58.120
Really?

01:24:58.120 --> 01:25:02.030
The new version of After FX that just came out is very powerful.

01:25:02.030 --> 01:25:04.820
I thought they changed a lot. Did you already learn it?

01:25:04.820 --> 01:25:07.730
That's amazing. You're pretty talented.

01:25:07.730 --> 01:25:10.260
All right, let's go over it, shall we?

01:25:10.260 --> 01:25:13.670
It's an underwater explosion, so it should be a mix of air and water.

01:25:13.670 --> 01:25:17.420
But it's the starting point of the story, so I want it as flashy as possible.

01:25:17.420 --> 01:25:21.260
How about sending debris flying, to give the scene more depth?

01:25:21.260 --> 01:25:22.930
By all means!

01:25:28.560 --> 01:25:30.770
Hello, everyone.

01:25:31.250 --> 01:25:36.150
Today, I've brought along some ladies who know a lot about drawing.

01:25:36.150 --> 01:25:37.400
Come on out.

01:25:44.970 --> 01:25:48.290
Hello, I'm the MC lady!

01:25:51.310 --> 01:25:55.420
Today we'll be making animation out of your drawings!

01:25:55.420 --> 01:25:58.050
The animations that you see on TV

01:25:58.050 --> 01:26:01.010
are actually a lot of different drawings shown in sequence—

01:26:01.010 --> 01:26:02.880
I don't get what you're talking about!

01:26:02.250 --> 01:26:04.290
You're boring!

01:26:02.880 --> 01:26:06.090
Don't you have something more funny to say?

01:26:04.290 --> 01:26:06.090
Can I go outside and play?

01:26:06.090 --> 01:26:07.990
Remember the children's attention span, Oi.

01:26:07.990 --> 01:26:09.840
No more than three lines at a time!

01:26:11.510 --> 01:26:14.640
Well, today we'll be making your drawings move!

01:26:14.640 --> 01:26:15.560
What?

01:26:14.640 --> 01:26:16.450
What do you mean?

01:26:15.560 --> 01:26:17.440
Seriously?! How?!

01:26:16.450 --> 01:26:18.770
Don't let them fool you! As if drawings can move!

01:26:19.070 --> 01:26:20.860
Hey, hey, what's this thing?

01:26:20.860 --> 01:26:23.400
It's a keyframe. It's what anime is made from.

01:26:23.400 --> 01:26:25.740
But I guess it's a bit too hard for you kids.

01:26:25.740 --> 01:26:27.370
Screw you! I'll do it!

01:26:27.370 --> 01:26:30.840
Are you sure? You have to draw a line between the points in order.

01:26:30.840 --> 01:26:33.160
Hey, this is a piece of cake!

01:26:32.410 --> 01:26:33.680
Can't believe he fell for it.

01:26:33.160 --> 01:26:35.040
Really? I think it's pretty difficult.

01:26:35.040 --> 01:26:37.500
Yeah, right! I'm awesome at concentrating, this is nothing!

01:26:37.500 --> 01:26:38.380
I wanna do it too!

01:26:38.380 --> 01:26:39.250
Me too!

01:26:39.250 --> 01:26:39.920
Me three!

01:26:39.920 --> 01:26:40.920
Me four!

01:26:40.920 --> 01:26:42.510
What'cha doing?

01:26:42.510 --> 01:26:44.630
I'm combining all of your drawings.

01:26:44.630 --> 01:26:45.720
How?

01:26:45.720 --> 01:26:49.710
I don't mind showing you, as long help me out.

01:26:49.710 --> 01:26:51.390
What? No way.

01:26:50.600 --> 01:26:51.390
No way.

01:26:51.390 --> 01:26:55.770
Why not? I'm sure it would be much more fun if we all did it together.

01:26:55.770 --> 01:27:00.190
Well, if you <i>really</i> want us to, I guess we could help.

01:27:02.180 --> 01:27:04.530
Great, let's split the work! The two of you will...

01:27:04.530 --> 01:27:06.150
Okay, everyone, gather around!

01:27:06.150 --> 01:27:08.700
Your anime is about to start!

01:27:11.190 --> 01:27:12.000
The heck?

01:27:12.000 --> 01:27:13.190
I drew that one.

01:27:13.190 --> 01:27:15.020
It's not moving.

01:27:16.250 --> 01:27:18.030
It's true! It's moving!

01:27:27.340 --> 01:27:28.260
What?

01:27:27.830 --> 01:27:29.280
Seriously?!

01:27:28.260 --> 01:27:30.510
Hey, I know who that is!

01:27:29.280 --> 01:27:31.710
Get a grip! As if!

01:27:34.940 --> 01:27:36.980
Do you kids know me?

01:27:36.980 --> 01:27:39.310
Namenamero!

01:27:39.310 --> 01:27:42.360
Great! You sure know your stuff, kids.

01:27:42.360 --> 01:27:44.080
Let's move on to my next question.

01:27:44.080 --> 01:27:48.780
My mommy is a mackerel fish, my daddy is a miso lord, and my little sister is...

01:27:48.780 --> 01:27:51.200
Sweet sushi sister!

01:27:50.010 --> 01:27:51.200
Bingo!

01:27:51.200 --> 01:27:52.700
You kids are awesome!

01:27:52.700 --> 01:27:55.630
Thanks for making me into anime, licky-licky.

01:27:55.630 --> 01:27:58.490
We're gonna raise the roof, so don't mess with me.

01:27:58.490 --> 01:28:00.710
It's Name Name March time!

01:28:04.700 --> 01:28:06.760
Stomp-stomp name-name, stomp-stomp name-name

01:28:06.760 --> 01:28:08.590
Stomp-stomp name-name, stomp-name stomp-stomp

01:28:08.590 --> 01:28:10.610
Stomp-name stomp-stomp-stomp

01:28:10.610 --> 01:28:12.680
Name-namero, name-namero

01:28:12.680 --> 01:28:14.750
Name-name-namero

01:28:14.750 --> 01:28:18.660
Fillet it, chop it, shred it, sticky-sticky (name!)

01:28:18.660 --> 01:28:20.750
Don't mess with me, namero

01:28:20.750 --> 01:28:22.640
If you mess with me, perarinpyo

01:28:22.640 --> 01:28:24.680
Don't mess with me, namero

01:28:24.680 --> 01:28:26.670
I'll turn you into fishflakes (name!)

01:28:35.270 --> 01:28:39.370
Drawing isn't about logic. It's about instincts.

01:28:39.780 --> 01:28:42.150
Having fun, being happy...

01:28:42.150 --> 01:28:48.380
Perhaps the reason I'm doing this is to have the children teach me how to do that.

01:28:51.210 --> 01:28:53.820
That was kind of incredible.

01:28:54.500 --> 01:28:56.040
They overwhelmed me.

01:28:56.040 --> 01:28:57.440
They taught me things.

01:28:57.440 --> 01:28:58.890
They made me happy.

01:28:59.320 --> 01:29:00.830
They cheered me up.

01:29:12.270 --> 01:29:13.160
Okudo.

01:29:13.580 --> 01:29:17.620
Would you mind doing the part where the water pipes break and water gushes out?

01:29:17.620 --> 01:29:18.080
Huh?

01:29:18.080 --> 01:29:22.330
You'd put out much better work, quicker than I could.

01:29:22.830 --> 01:29:23.670
Okay!

01:29:24.390 --> 01:29:25.670
Really?!

01:29:25.970 --> 01:29:27.550
Thank you so much!

01:29:27.550 --> 01:29:30.060
Are you stopping by Yasuhara's place today?

01:29:30.060 --> 01:29:33.410
While the sun may already be setting, I fully intend to call on her.

01:29:33.410 --> 01:29:34.930
Mind telling her something from me?

01:29:34.930 --> 01:29:36.180
Anything you require!

01:29:36.180 --> 01:29:38.180
No, it's not that big of a deal.

01:29:38.730 --> 01:29:42.540
Tell her I'm watching forward to seeing her part during QA.

01:29:43.180 --> 01:29:44.440
Understood, sir!

01:29:45.200 --> 01:29:47.290
I could never accept it.

01:29:47.290 --> 01:29:49.690
Why can't we go where we want freely?

01:29:50.310 --> 01:29:52.780
Why is there a limit to what we can do?

01:29:53.410 --> 01:29:57.200
Why do we have dreams that we're not even permitted to have?

01:29:57.640 --> 01:30:00.920
But no one would give me an answer.

01:30:00.920 --> 01:30:03.540
Before long, I stopped thinking for myself,

01:30:03.540 --> 01:30:06.520
just going through the motions of life.

01:30:06.520 --> 01:30:11.380
I thought every day would be the same as the last, to finally come to a quiet end one day.

01:30:13.660 --> 01:30:17.370
But Raul and Hedwig taught me.

01:30:18.100 --> 01:30:19.810
No two days are the same.

01:30:19.810 --> 01:30:21.720
Tomorrow a new day awaits us!

01:30:22.770 --> 01:30:26.560
So why are you all giving up?

01:30:26.560 --> 01:30:27.690
Let's go!

01:30:27.960 --> 01:30:30.870
There's no telling if we'll succeed,

01:30:30.870 --> 01:30:33.240
but we have to march on toward our dream!

01:30:33.240 --> 01:30:36.930
To fight and struggle toward our future!

01:30:41.200 --> 01:30:43.200
I'm sorry, I just...

01:30:43.200 --> 01:30:44.430
Don't worry, I understand.

01:30:44.430 --> 01:30:45.960
It's great isn't it? I'm tearing up.

01:30:45.960 --> 01:30:48.850
She turned out far more complex than I expected!

01:30:48.850 --> 01:30:49.780
Yeah.

01:30:49.780 --> 01:30:53.810
When I found myself captivated by Arte's negative emotions during the audition,

01:30:53.810 --> 01:30:55.470
I finally felt like I could do this.

01:30:55.880 --> 01:30:58.720
You shouldn't decide what someone is capable of before giving them a chance.

01:30:58.720 --> 01:31:00.500
Absolutely.

01:31:01.180 --> 01:31:03.360
Turn your phone off in the studio.

01:31:03.360 --> 01:31:05.120
Sorry about that, I forgot.

01:31:06.140 --> 01:31:07.060
Something the matter?

01:31:07.060 --> 01:31:08.890
N-No, it's nothing!

01:31:08.890 --> 01:31:10.360
Let's keep going.

01:31:10.360 --> 01:31:11.440
All righty.

01:31:12.780 --> 01:31:14.190
Cheers!

01:31:14.190 --> 01:31:17.070
I'm terribly sorry about calling you all the way here.

01:31:17.070 --> 01:31:17.950
And?

01:31:17.950 --> 01:31:21.500
My, how scary. I have something important to discuss, you know.

01:31:21.500 --> 01:31:24.330
Katsuragi, you're making SIVA, aren't you?

01:31:24.330 --> 01:31:29.080
That IP doesn't just belong to you, but to us too, correct?

01:31:31.040 --> 01:31:33.210
You're one to talk!

01:31:33.210 --> 01:31:35.970
I'm sorry, but you're bothering the other guests.

01:31:36.510 --> 01:31:37.900
I'm sorry.

01:31:38.410 --> 01:31:41.850
I didn't expect to get thrown out of GePeU.

01:31:41.850 --> 01:31:44.600
Didn't you break some crystal decoration?

01:31:44.600 --> 01:31:45.930
That was an accident...

01:31:45.930 --> 01:31:47.480
That's enough for a ban.

01:31:47.480 --> 01:31:52.360
So, what do they want? For us to end production and stop using their title, I imagine?

01:31:52.360 --> 01:31:53.310
What?!

01:31:53.310 --> 01:31:56.330
Well, there's no excusing that we're using the same title.

01:31:56.330 --> 01:31:57.270
Pretty much.

01:31:57.270 --> 01:31:59.250
How come we didn't change it?

01:31:59.250 --> 01:32:02.240
There was already a teaser out using the name.

01:32:02.860 --> 01:32:05.240
There's even a small copyright notice and all.

01:32:05.240 --> 01:32:08.040
What are their demands? Stopping the screening?

01:32:08.790 --> 01:32:10.630
Do they have the right to do that?

01:32:10.630 --> 01:32:13.630
Our legal department is currently in talks with them.

01:32:13.630 --> 01:32:15.720
As unfounded as it may be,

01:32:15.720 --> 01:32:18.820
we can't just ignore their complaints and screen it anyway.

01:32:18.820 --> 01:32:21.680
But we also don't have time to wait for things to get sorted out.

01:32:21.680 --> 01:32:24.760
What are they after? Royalties?

01:32:24.760 --> 01:32:28.640
I bet they want to make it a joint production
and become the lead studio.

01:32:28.640 --> 01:32:31.300
They get all the rights, and we become subcontractors.

01:32:31.300 --> 01:32:33.520
What?! But they're the ones who stepped down!

01:32:33.520 --> 01:32:38.210
If they claim that they were removed unilaterally and that they planned to finish it,

01:32:38.210 --> 01:32:39.780
we'll look like the bad guys.

01:32:41.670 --> 01:32:43.780
I should have been more careful.

01:32:44.640 --> 01:32:46.090
I'm really sorry.

01:33:59.070 --> 01:34:01.170
We're halting production.

01:34:03.700 --> 01:34:07.950
I knew it. No way they'd be able to handle a real project.

01:34:07.120 --> 01:34:08.590
Well, obviously.

01:34:07.950 --> 01:34:09.420
I mean, it's Musani.

01:34:09.420 --> 01:34:11.040
Yeah, it's Musani.

01:34:10.000 --> 01:34:11.950
It's still Musani.

01:34:11.040 --> 01:34:13.080
Man, good thing I didn't take the offer.

01:34:13.080 --> 01:34:15.940
I knew it'd end up like this. It's Musani, after all.

01:34:23.050 --> 01:34:25.520
It's... all over...

01:34:25.520 --> 01:34:26.590
Three, two...

01:34:27.940 --> 01:34:29.700
Stop acting like a baby!

01:34:29.700 --> 01:34:32.250
What are you doing wallowing in depression?

01:34:32.250 --> 01:34:34.940
It's not over yet. If anything, it's just getting started.

01:34:34.940 --> 01:34:38.060
You're a producer, aren't you? Get ahold of yourself!

01:34:38.060 --> 01:34:39.440
A producer...

01:34:39.440 --> 01:34:43.360
That's right. What's the most important thing to a producer?

01:34:44.300 --> 01:34:48.200
I said, what's the most important thing to a producer?!

01:34:48.200 --> 01:34:49.980
Think carefully, producer.

01:34:49.980 --> 01:34:50.830
Think.

01:34:51.720 --> 01:34:52.760
The work?

01:34:52.760 --> 01:34:53.960
Is that all?

01:34:53.960 --> 01:34:55.010
The staff?

01:34:55.010 --> 01:34:56.570
And?

01:34:56.570 --> 01:34:58.750
The budget, the schedule...

01:34:59.410 --> 01:35:00.340
The quality.

01:35:00.340 --> 01:35:00.960
Great!

01:35:00.960 --> 01:35:01.710
That's not all.

01:35:01.710 --> 01:35:02.580
Huh?

01:35:02.580 --> 01:35:05.840
The most important thing to a producer

01:35:06.240 --> 01:35:08.970
is to finish the work.

01:35:08.970 --> 01:35:12.640
And to show it to the viewers.

01:35:27.250 --> 01:35:28.910
Are you planning on going like that?

01:35:30.070 --> 01:35:31.330
Okitsu!

01:35:34.660 --> 01:35:37.370
We never got a chance to use it for Time Hippo.

01:35:50.130 --> 01:35:51.760
You should have asked me.

01:35:51.760 --> 01:35:54.100
Did you forget about the drinks of sisterhood

01:35:55.370 --> 01:35:57.100
we shared in Ogikubo?

01:35:57.100 --> 01:36:00.740
You have my gratitude. I swear to repay you one day.

01:36:00.740 --> 01:36:03.110
You can repay me with SIVA.

01:36:21.440 --> 01:36:23.380
Wait! You can't come in here!

01:36:23.640 --> 01:36:25.750
Hey! Wait!

01:36:26.180 --> 01:36:29.510
Stop right there! Where do you think you are?

01:36:29.510 --> 01:36:33.710
This is the base of the honored GePeU clan!

01:36:35.780 --> 01:36:37.220
Have at them!

01:36:37.700 --> 01:36:40.780
Time for digital outsourcing again!

01:36:42.520 --> 01:36:46.070
Outsource everything! Outsource everything! Outsource every—

01:36:46.070 --> 01:36:48.530
Animation directors are there to be skipped!

01:36:48.910 --> 01:36:49.810
How dare you?!

01:36:49.810 --> 01:36:51.530
Have at them, have at them!

01:37:05.960 --> 01:37:08.010
It's the director's job to delay!

01:37:06.710 --> 01:37:08.800
We're in the red! We're in the red! We're in the red!

01:37:08.010 --> 01:37:10.140
Twelve hours until air!

01:37:09.040 --> 01:37:11.260
The server crashed!

01:37:09.730 --> 01:37:11.930
Who cares about the quality?!

01:37:10.470 --> 01:37:12.710
Fixing retakes is just wasted time!

01:37:11.830 --> 01:37:14.160
We can finish it in a week!

01:37:11.970 --> 01:37:14.560
Who's even watching this anime?!

01:37:12.890 --> 01:37:14.560
Just wing it for now!

01:37:44.040 --> 01:37:44.080
Guest

01:37:58.750 --> 01:38:01.430
No, you can't do that!

01:38:01.430 --> 01:38:02.490
Wait for me!

01:38:10.520 --> 01:38:13.460
You can't expect me to tear up the contract, now can you?

01:38:13.460 --> 01:38:16.000
The contract has yet to be signed, correct?

01:38:16.000 --> 01:38:18.120
In other words, it hasn't yet taken effect.

01:38:18.120 --> 01:38:21.250
Oh? Now that's a bold claim.

01:38:21.250 --> 01:38:25.960
This document only exists to begin with because the two companies came to a mutual agreement.

01:38:25.960 --> 01:38:28.270
Saying the lack of a signature means it's void

01:38:28.270 --> 01:38:31.630
doesn't quite seem in line with standard business practice.

01:38:31.970 --> 01:38:36.320
In addition, the production was announced publicly, and an official website was put in place.

01:38:36.320 --> 01:38:41.010
And you claim that we have no rights just because the contract hasn't been signed?

01:38:41.900 --> 01:38:45.280
Now that's a bit cruel, don't you think?

01:38:46.120 --> 01:38:49.320
I'm sorry for making you waste your time, but I would appreciate it if—

01:38:49.320 --> 01:38:51.480
If you wish to discuss responsibilities,

01:38:52.050 --> 01:38:54.490
you, too, have responsibilities of your own.

01:38:54.490 --> 01:38:55.580
Excuse me?

01:38:55.580 --> 01:38:58.120
It's important to show your sincerity.

01:38:58.120 --> 01:39:02.690
The producer entrusts the studio with a work,
and the studio responds in kind with a finished work.

01:39:02.690 --> 01:39:04.000
Sincerity?

01:39:04.000 --> 01:39:05.830
In making the work.

01:39:05.830 --> 01:39:07.790
And we did make it!

01:39:07.790 --> 01:39:09.330
From what I heard,

01:39:09.330 --> 01:39:11.760
the director finished two pages of storyboards.

01:39:11.760 --> 01:39:12.550
See?

01:39:12.550 --> 01:39:16.650
However, having announced it publicly, you can't simply ignore the deadline.

01:39:17.280 --> 01:39:21.640
Schedules are always put together with the assumption that there will be delays.

01:39:22.210 --> 01:39:23.270
Resorting to violence?

01:39:28.930 --> 01:39:35.360
The minutes of a January 20, 2017 meeting
state that Western Entertainment contracted GePeU

01:39:35.360 --> 01:39:41.530
to deliver the requested product in accordance with the schedule listed at the end of the contract.

01:39:41.530 --> 01:39:48.040
The schedule, in turn, says that the storyboards must be delivered before the end of February 2019.

01:39:48.040 --> 01:39:51.270
And in article 12, section 1 of this contract, it says,

01:39:51.270 --> 01:39:56.800
"Party A, GePeU Inc., and party B,
Western Entertainment Inc.,

01:39:56.800 --> 01:40:00.970
will, in the event that the other party has violated the contract or associated agreements,

01:40:00.970 --> 01:40:06.030
consult with the other party in order to resolve the violation within an appropriate amount of time,

01:40:06.030 --> 01:40:10.940
and if the violation is not resolved within that period, this contract may be revoked."

01:40:11.200 --> 01:40:12.440
And section 2 says,

01:40:12.440 --> 01:40:19.680
"If, due to a cause attributable to party A,
the completion of the product is impeded,

01:40:19.680 --> 01:40:24.120
party B may revoke this contract after promptly informing party A."

01:40:24.120 --> 01:40:27.190
I can't say I remember seeing such a schedule.

01:40:27.190 --> 01:40:30.360
<i>The deal was that you'd spend two years and have it ready one year before the premiere!</i>

01:40:30.360 --> 01:40:32.670
<i>Come on, just wait another month.</i>

01:40:32.670 --> 01:40:36.590
<i>Another month or two doesn't make much of a difference, right?</i>

01:40:36.590 --> 01:40:38.140
<i>It absolutely does!</i>

01:40:38.140 --> 01:40:39.550
Although...

01:40:39.550 --> 01:40:43.350
We might be able to figure something out if you give us a bigger budget.

01:40:41.340 --> 01:40:42.010
Wait, that's...

01:40:43.350 --> 01:40:46.280
I hope you won't let us down.

01:40:44.250 --> 01:40:48.490
This audio was recorded with a voice recorder inside my colleague Katsuragi's bag.

01:40:48.490 --> 01:40:50.480
That's illegal! You can't use that!

01:40:50.480 --> 01:40:52.730
Feel free to make that claim.

01:40:53.440 --> 01:40:54.310
In court.

01:40:54.310 --> 01:40:54.820
In co—

01:40:59.610 --> 01:41:02.320
We have an understanding, yes?

01:41:06.830 --> 01:41:08.330
We do, yes?

01:41:47.160 --> 01:41:49.490
Ooyama Takumi
Sound Effects

01:41:54.840 --> 01:41:56.590
Director, what do you think?

01:41:58.040 --> 01:42:01.170
Well... I think it should be fine.

01:42:01.170 --> 01:42:03.630
Does anyone else have any comment?

01:42:04.930 --> 01:42:10.220
All right, with that, the mixing of Amphibious Assault Ship SIVA is complete.

01:42:10.220 --> 01:42:11.310
Congratulations.

01:42:11.310 --> 01:42:13.560
Congratulations!

01:42:14.310 --> 01:42:16.360
I thought it'd take longer.

01:42:16.360 --> 01:42:18.320
Yeah, we're an hour ahead of schedule.

01:42:18.320 --> 01:42:20.860
You all did great! Thank you so much!

01:42:20.860 --> 01:42:25.070
Personally, I wish we could've gotten one more minute of the climax.

01:42:25.720 --> 01:42:28.340
It's a bit anticlimactic, huh?

01:42:28.340 --> 01:42:31.090
No, no, what are you saying? It's a great movie!

01:42:31.090 --> 01:42:32.830
It's a miracle that we made it here!

01:42:32.830 --> 01:42:35.140
Everything turned out great! Just great!

01:42:35.140 --> 01:42:36.210
I'm heading out, then.

01:42:36.210 --> 01:42:37.170
See you.

01:42:37.170 --> 01:42:38.590
Bye!

01:42:40.930 --> 01:42:43.660
Why don't they have some food before leaving?

01:42:43.660 --> 01:42:47.320
They said they'd have a small celebration party, since they're done for the day.

01:42:47.320 --> 01:42:49.140
All this eel going to waste...

01:42:49.610 --> 01:42:54.350
They were so insistent on having eel when we went location scouting in Hamamatsu. What gives?

01:43:18.420 --> 01:43:22.630
Additional participants,
contact Miyamori

01:43:18.420 --> 01:43:22.630
The release
party is
finally here!!

01:43:28.180 --> 01:43:29.720
U-Um, this is...

01:43:30.010 --> 01:43:33.100
I suddenly felt like having some curry. You know, like before.

01:43:33.100 --> 01:43:35.240
When the president would make some for us.

01:43:35.240 --> 01:43:36.560
His curry was great, wasn't it?

01:43:36.560 --> 01:43:37.730
It sure was.

01:43:37.730 --> 01:43:40.450
Oh, Miyamori, would you mind tasting it?

01:43:42.470 --> 01:43:43.850
What do you think?

01:43:44.710 --> 01:43:45.750
It's good.

01:43:45.750 --> 01:43:46.810
Really?

01:43:47.340 --> 01:43:49.150
What's the matter?

01:43:49.150 --> 01:43:51.740
It's just... Something's missing, isn't it?

01:43:52.910 --> 01:43:56.400
Are you talking about the curry? Or about SIVA?

01:43:58.950 --> 01:44:01.520
Well, both, I guess, but...

01:44:01.520 --> 01:44:04.240
You're not satisfied with the SIVA you saw today, are you?

01:44:04.240 --> 01:44:08.470
That's, uh... Not super satisfied and super happy, I guess,

01:44:08.470 --> 01:44:09.580
but it's more or less what I—

01:44:09.580 --> 01:44:11.760
Then what's missing, exactly?

01:44:14.220 --> 01:44:16.270
Why won't you say anything?

01:44:23.790 --> 01:44:26.280
Thank you all for your hard work.

01:44:26.280 --> 01:44:29.490
You all did your best in spite of the impossible schedule,

01:44:29.490 --> 01:44:31.780
and thanks to you, we've made it through mixing.

01:44:31.780 --> 01:44:33.170
Thank you so much.

01:44:33.170 --> 01:44:34.600
So much.

01:44:34.600 --> 01:44:38.040
But I'd like to share my own opinion for a moment.

01:44:38.500 --> 01:44:42.690
I do think the story works as it is already.

01:44:42.690 --> 01:44:46.500
The early and middle parts are well-paced, and it's truly enjoyable to watch.

01:44:46.800 --> 01:44:50.040
However, toward the end, it becomes too fast-paced,

01:44:50.040 --> 01:44:54.200
the plot moves too quickly, and the climax feels somewhat empty.

01:44:54.200 --> 01:44:57.850
Perhaps I'm the only one here who thinks this way.

01:44:58.380 --> 01:45:00.070
What about you all?

01:45:00.070 --> 01:45:01.900
Please, tell me what you think.

01:45:03.250 --> 01:45:07.100
Can I just share my impression?
Like, from an objective perspective.

01:45:07.100 --> 01:45:07.820
Yes.

01:45:07.820 --> 01:45:10.470
Do you want good impressions or bad impressions?

01:45:10.470 --> 01:45:11.320
Either one.

01:45:11.320 --> 01:45:14.030
Bad impressions, in other words.

01:45:15.500 --> 01:45:17.990
I agree that the climax was way too rushed.

01:45:17.990 --> 01:45:20.860
It felt like the music carried the movie at the end.

01:45:20.860 --> 01:45:23.710
It's like it ended just as it was about to begin.

01:45:23.710 --> 01:45:27.080
So it's not bad, but it's like something's missing.

01:45:27.080 --> 01:45:27.880
Something...

01:45:27.880 --> 01:45:28.780
Needs more flair.

01:45:29.550 --> 01:45:33.100
Yeah, I know, but the point is it's a bit late now.

01:45:33.100 --> 01:45:34.600
Yeah, I guess so.

01:45:34.600 --> 01:45:35.850
Well, about that...

01:45:36.880 --> 01:45:38.410
I agree that it's late now.

01:45:38.410 --> 01:45:41.300
It's late, but this is its final version.

01:45:41.300 --> 01:45:44.290
It's the final form which will be shown on the big screen.

01:45:44.290 --> 01:45:47.830
Are you all really fine with that?

01:45:47.830 --> 01:45:49.730
So, what are you trying to say?

01:45:50.110 --> 01:45:52.490
I want to remake the final part.

01:45:53.530 --> 01:45:55.490
Hey, h-h-hold up there, Miyamori.

01:45:55.490 --> 01:45:59.750
I got carried away back there when we talked about remaking it,

01:45:59.750 --> 01:46:01.580
but forget that ever happened.

01:46:01.580 --> 01:46:04.000
I'm really sorry, everyone. It's fine, I'm happy with it.

01:46:04.000 --> 01:46:05.580
Are you really happy with it?

01:46:05.930 --> 01:46:07.110
Really, truly?

01:46:16.520 --> 01:46:18.470
Sail toward our future.

01:46:18.470 --> 01:46:19.860
Full speed ahead!

01:46:34.070 --> 01:46:37.070
Well, it's certainly underwhelming from a dramatic standpoint.

01:46:37.070 --> 01:46:40.200
There's definitely a lack of catharsis.

01:46:40.200 --> 01:46:42.500
We only have three weeks until the premiere.

01:46:42.500 --> 01:46:44.570
No way we've got time to remake it.

01:46:44.570 --> 01:46:47.350
Let's just call it quits already, guys. I'm happy with—

01:46:47.350 --> 01:46:51.670
It's not a question of if <i>you're</i> happy with it, but if the viewers are.

01:46:51.670 --> 01:46:55.250
I'm sick of my work going unfinished.

01:46:55.250 --> 01:46:58.270
What if it ends up like Time Hippo?

01:46:58.270 --> 01:47:02.520
Some things can't be solved through sheer willpower alone.

01:47:02.520 --> 01:47:03.810
I'm aware.

01:47:06.520 --> 01:47:08.520
Well, as long as you're aware.

01:47:08.520 --> 01:47:10.110
Make the decision, Director.

01:47:10.110 --> 01:47:10.990
Why me?!

01:47:10.990 --> 01:47:12.550
Well, you're the director!

01:47:12.550 --> 01:47:13.610
Please decide.

01:47:13.610 --> 01:47:14.800
We'll go along with whatever you say.

01:47:14.800 --> 01:47:17.590
Isn't this something the president, Watanabe, should decide?

01:47:17.590 --> 01:47:18.700
I'll leave it to the producer.

01:47:18.700 --> 01:47:21.130
Director Kinoshita, please!

01:47:21.130 --> 01:47:24.250
For the sake of SIVA, and the people coming to view it.

01:47:25.130 --> 01:47:30.370
To be honest, when I saw it during mixing, it felt kind of lacking.

01:47:30.370 --> 01:47:37.170
But it's awful to even <i>think</i> about whether this really is what I wanted to make.

01:47:37.170 --> 01:47:39.610
Hellish, even.

01:47:39.610 --> 01:47:44.080
We just finished it, so it doesn't feel right to throw away all this work.

01:47:44.080 --> 01:47:48.460
If it turns out worse than what I imagine, if it just comes out half-baked,

01:47:48.460 --> 01:47:51.170
then maybe it's better not to do it at all...

01:47:52.590 --> 01:47:55.140
What the hell is that? You're seriously pissing me off.

01:47:56.010 --> 01:47:58.530
In that case, just give us the storyboards!

01:47:58.800 --> 01:48:01.660
We'll make something even better than what you imagine!

01:48:02.790 --> 01:48:04.580
Endou, you're so cool!

01:48:04.580 --> 01:48:05.410
Shut up.

01:48:05.900 --> 01:48:10.370
Please, lend us your help just a bit longer!

01:48:10.890 --> 01:48:11.920
Longer!

01:48:11.920 --> 01:48:15.760
Director, this isn't the time for begging.

01:48:15.760 --> 01:48:16.820
I have no objections.

01:48:16.820 --> 01:48:18.110
You owe me for this, okay?

01:48:18.110 --> 01:48:20.390
I was planning on getting a haircut, you know.

01:48:20.390 --> 01:48:22.640
I can't just abandon ship now!

01:48:25.060 --> 01:48:27.600
Set sights for the final stretch, full speed ahead!

01:48:27.860 --> 01:48:29.600
Full speed ahead!

01:48:30.440 --> 01:48:34.820
Premiere Day

01:48:33.010 --> 01:48:34.820
Oh, SIVA?

01:48:34.820 --> 01:48:36.960
What kind of movie is it?

01:48:36.960 --> 01:48:41.990
A hot-head, a slacker, a cool cucumber, and a crybaby

01:48:41.990 --> 01:48:45.510
all come together in search of a new world.

01:48:45.510 --> 01:48:48.200
It's about fighting for what you want.

01:48:48.200 --> 01:48:49.950
So they're fighting.

01:48:49.950 --> 01:48:50.830
They're fighting.

01:48:52.200 --> 01:48:55.360
It embodies everything that Musani is right now.

01:49:00.850 --> 01:49:04.860
Do you really have time to be here today? It's premiere day.

01:49:04.860 --> 01:49:07.720
Only Raul and Hedwig will be on stage today.

01:49:07.720 --> 01:49:09.080
I'm next week.

01:49:09.080 --> 01:49:12.210
Zuka's gonna be in the news online, isn't she?

01:49:12.210 --> 01:49:13.580
I'll have a look!

01:49:14.660 --> 01:49:16.020
Everyone, got one?

01:49:16.020 --> 01:49:16.900
Yeah.

01:49:16.900 --> 01:49:17.780
Yup!

01:49:18.650 --> 01:49:19.570
Right here.

01:49:20.320 --> 01:49:21.980
Don-don-donuts!

01:49:21.980 --> 01:49:23.570
Let's go nuts!

01:49:47.940 --> 01:49:48.990
They'll break through it.

01:49:48.990 --> 01:49:49.640
Yep.

01:49:49.950 --> 01:49:51.490
Kouyou, you bastard!

01:49:51.490 --> 01:49:53.750
He's refusing to let any underground dwellers flee!

01:49:53.750 --> 01:49:55.430
I guess that's it for SIVA here.

01:49:55.430 --> 01:49:58.280
Hedwig, what do we do? Is it all over?

01:49:58.280 --> 01:50:00.620
Don't be stupid. Tomato, we're escaping.

01:50:00.620 --> 01:50:01.140
Right!

01:50:01.140 --> 01:50:03.250
But it's a long way to the escape hatch.

01:50:03.250 --> 01:50:04.780
They'll catch up with us before then.

01:50:04.780 --> 01:50:05.620
I know.

01:50:06.120 --> 01:50:07.530
Raul. Let's go.

01:50:08.980 --> 01:50:11.620
You got it! I'll struggle with all I've got!

01:50:11.620 --> 01:50:14.620
Give me a break. Don't count me out of that for a damn second.

01:50:14.620 --> 01:50:17.880
We're friends, aren't we? I, Heartful, will help out too!

01:50:17.880 --> 01:50:19.960
And I can fight when it really counts!

01:50:19.960 --> 01:50:22.620
Pegacorns, full speed toward the escape hatch!

01:50:22.620 --> 01:50:24.220
All right, fine, I know!

01:50:24.220 --> 01:50:25.970
Don't treat us like workhorses!

01:50:25.970 --> 01:50:28.720
We're not horses! We're pegacorns!

01:50:28.720 --> 01:50:31.370
Arte, I'm leaving the brats to you.

01:50:31.370 --> 01:50:33.940
Make your own luck, and seize the way to your homeland.

01:50:35.480 --> 01:50:38.150
All right. I swear I'll seize it with my own hands.

01:50:38.150 --> 01:50:39.650
Because there's no such thing as a miracle!

01:50:41.650 --> 01:50:43.270
Go, go! Don't look back!

01:50:43.270 --> 01:50:44.450
Faster, faster!

01:50:47.410 --> 01:50:49.340
Sail toward our future.

01:50:49.340 --> 01:50:50.740
Full speed ahead!

01:51:11.990 --> 01:51:12.950
Kouyou!

01:51:12.950 --> 01:51:15.980
How dare you approach the mighty Captain Kouyou,
you filthy underground dweller!

01:51:15.980 --> 01:51:19.430
Fight as much as you want,
but you can't change this world!

01:51:19.430 --> 01:51:20.980
Stop struggling in vain!

01:51:20.360 --> 01:51:21.800
I'll never stop!

01:51:32.190 --> 01:51:33.290
I won't run!

01:51:53.760 --> 01:51:54.680
They're in trouble!

01:51:54.680 --> 01:51:57.190
I'll fight them off here, you go help Arte!

01:51:56.310 --> 01:51:57.190
Hurry up!

01:52:00.170 --> 01:52:00.770
Hit it!

01:52:00.770 --> 01:52:01.800
Obviously!

01:52:13.160 --> 01:52:17.500
I wonder what our homeland's like. Never seen it myself.

01:52:17.840 --> 01:52:20.210
Well, there's a ton of tasty food to eat!

01:52:20.210 --> 01:52:21.920
The sky's beautiful.

01:52:21.920 --> 01:52:23.670
There's no fighting.

01:52:23.670 --> 01:52:26.170
It's a place where everyone is smiling.

01:52:29.180 --> 01:52:31.180
It's fine. Everything will be just fine.

01:52:31.560 --> 01:52:33.720
Just one more kilometer! Hang in there!

01:53:00.270 --> 01:53:01.230
Spread your wings!

01:53:01.230 --> 01:53:02.420
You got it!

01:53:12.430 --> 01:53:14.050
Don't let them escape!

01:53:17.060 --> 01:53:19.060
Kouyou!

01:53:44.560 --> 01:53:45.840
I won't miss this time.

01:54:03.050 --> 01:54:04.380
We did it.

01:54:05.130 --> 01:54:06.360
Serves you right.

01:54:06.360 --> 01:54:07.990
Now then, what do we do?

01:54:07.990 --> 01:54:09.360
Isn't that obvious?

01:54:10.860 --> 01:54:14.300
We'll fight our way through, steal their ship, and escape.

01:54:14.300 --> 01:54:15.570
Obviously.

01:54:30.160 --> 01:54:32.680
<i>Raul and Hedwig taught me.</i>

01:54:33.220 --> 01:54:36.840
<i>No two days are the same.
Tomorrow, a new day awaits us.</i>

01:54:37.510 --> 01:54:40.220
<i>So why are you all giving up?</i>

01:54:41.120 --> 01:54:42.350
<i>Let's go.</i>

01:54:42.350 --> 01:54:47.140
<i>There's no telling if we'll succeed, but we have to march on toward our dream.</i>

01:54:47.760 --> 01:54:51.030
<i>To fight and struggle toward the future.</i>

01:54:51.650 --> 01:54:54.610
<i>Sail toward our future,</i>

01:54:55.210 --> 01:54:56.270
<i>full speed ahead.</i>

01:55:09.080 --> 01:55:12.800
Wearing magical shoes on our feet

01:55:12.800 --> 01:55:16.780
We run around until they're worn down

01:55:16.780 --> 01:55:20.470
As I work I find myself hoping

01:55:20.470 --> 01:55:23.860
That a miracle might suddenly occur

01:55:23.860 --> 01:55:27.840
Like a magical lamp

01:55:27.840 --> 01:55:31.770
That grants any wish

01:55:31.770 --> 01:55:35.910
Like a fairy tale

01:55:35.910 --> 01:55:39.900
Where the whole world is transformed in one night

01:55:39.900 --> 01:55:43.870
Let's find a wonder capable of that

01:55:43.870 --> 01:55:46.460
Collect the stars

01:55:46.460 --> 01:55:51.500
Assemble the fallen light

01:55:51.500 --> 01:55:54.130
In that moment

01:55:54.130 --> 01:55:59.960
I traced that twinkling shape

01:55:59.960 --> 01:56:05.930
And put it away in a box, see?

01:56:05.930 --> 01:56:10.460
This pattern will never fade

01:56:10.460 --> 01:56:20.370
Even if we were to be separated once more

01:56:22.080 --> 01:56:25.890
Your tears start to well up

01:56:25.890 --> 01:56:30.040
But even nights like these can become fond memories

01:56:30.040 --> 01:56:33.540
The hole opened in your heart

01:56:33.540 --> 01:56:37.160
It won't close, but you can still walk on

01:56:37.160 --> 01:56:40.930
A voice can be heard from somewhere

01:56:40.930 --> 01:56:44.600
Who is this message from?

01:56:44.600 --> 01:56:48.760
It whispers into your ear

01:56:48.760 --> 01:56:53.070
About the promise you made together that day

01:56:53.070 --> 01:56:55.820
Count the stars

01:56:55.820 --> 01:57:00.420
Draw a new constellation

01:57:00.420 --> 01:57:03.370
In that moment

01:57:03.370 --> 01:57:09.250
Countless dramas play out all at once

01:57:09.250 --> 01:57:14.930
And turn to crystal, see?

01:57:14.930 --> 01:57:21.050
This magic will never fade

01:57:34.520 --> 01:57:38.430
Even if you one day

01:57:38.430 --> 01:57:42.300
Came to lose

01:57:42.820 --> 01:57:50.420
Something precious to you, struck with grief

01:57:50.420 --> 01:57:57.940
In order to deliver as many wishes as I can

01:57:57.940 --> 01:58:02.040
I will continue to sing

01:58:02.040 --> 01:58:06.440
Taking this wonder into my hands

01:58:06.840 --> 01:58:09.680
Collect the stars

01:58:09.680 --> 01:58:14.460
Assemble the fallen light

01:58:14.460 --> 01:58:17.230
And then reach out

01:58:17.230 --> 01:58:22.200
Toward the fleeting, eternal light

01:58:22.200 --> 01:58:30.650
I trusted that this radiance would one day help you

01:58:30.650 --> 01:58:36.540
And put it away in a box, see?

01:58:36.540 --> 01:58:41.220
It's a dazzling miracle

01:58:41.220 --> 01:58:55.360
Even if we were to be separated once more

01:59:05.790 --> 01:59:07.200
Do you think it came across?

01:59:07.200 --> 01:59:08.330
What's "it"?

01:59:08.330 --> 01:59:10.370
Everything we wanted to get across.

01:59:10.370 --> 01:59:11.820
I don't know.

01:59:11.820 --> 01:59:13.970
You don't know?

01:59:13.970 --> 01:59:16.960
But I'm sure we put everything we could into it.

01:59:16.960 --> 01:59:17.790
Yeah!

01:59:18.390 --> 01:59:21.800
Today is ending, and tomorrow will come.

01:59:21.800 --> 01:59:23.000
I'm sure it will.

01:59:23.000 --> 01:59:24.650
What do you think it will be like?

01:59:24.650 --> 01:59:26.780
Better than today? Will it be a good day?

01:59:26.780 --> 01:59:29.170
Can we make it into a new, different day?

01:59:29.170 --> 01:59:34.260
I don't know, but if we fight and struggle, I'm sure it will change.

01:59:34.260 --> 01:59:37.650
To live is to experience an "only just begun" ending forever.

01:59:37.650 --> 01:59:40.630
"Our fight has only just begun," you mean?

01:59:40.630 --> 01:59:43.110
That's not particularly deep. Good grief.

01:59:43.750 --> 01:59:45.510
But it's not too bad.

01:59:46.800 --> 01:59:48.400
It's not too bad, yeah.

01:59:51.780 --> 01:59:53.080
Good morning.

